{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdZaUWdPjYVMNe53Qcdn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018EC2uytWyXCoVoLszmwh1T","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-repeat-z0r2wndt/7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff/tool-results/bsj8ssif6.txt","limit":700},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2530,"cache_read_input_tokens":15868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2530},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff","uuid":"4d036229-6e57-453f-8c39-6f2d050bbce2","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:24:03.333Z","request_id":"req_011CfdZaTtg6UQBKsDyPUjSq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018EC2uytWyXCoVoLszmwh1T":{"file_path":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-repeat-z0r2wndt/7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff/tool-results/bsj8ssif6.txt","limit":700}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018EC2uytWyXCoVoLszmwh1T","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=== README.md\n2\t     1\t# procurement-agent\n3\t     2\t\n4\t     3\tProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\n5\t     4\tinvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\n6\t     5\tpurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\n7\t     6\tvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n8\t     7\t\n9\t     8\t## Architecture\n10\t     9\t\n11\t    10\t```\n12\t    11\tmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\n13\t    12\tstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n14\t    13\t                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n15\t    14\t                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n16\t    15\t                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n17\t    16\t                                   |-- tools:\n18\t    17\t                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n19\t    18\t                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n20\t    19\t                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n21\t    20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n22\t    21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n23\t    22\t```\n24\t    23\t\n25\t    24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n26\t    25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n27\t    26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n28\t    27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n29\t    28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n30\t    29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n31\t    30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n32\t    31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n33\t    32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n34\t    33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n35\t    34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n36\t    35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n37\t    36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n38\t    37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n39\t    38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n40\t    39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n41\t    40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n42\t    41\t\n43\t    42\t## Context size\n44\t    43\t\n45\t    44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n46\t    45\t\n47\t    46\t| method | meaning |\n48\t    47\t|---|---|\n49\t    48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n50\t    49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n51\t    50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n52\t    51\t\n53\t    52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n54\t    53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n55\t    54\t\n56\t    55\t## Operating\n57\t    56\t\n58\t    57\t* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n59\t    58\t  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n60\t    59\t  start while a halt is set.\n61\t    60\t* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n62\t    61\t  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n63\t    62\t  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n64\t    63\t* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n65\t    64\t  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n66\t    65\t\n67\t    66\t## Tests\n68\t    67\t\n69\t    68\t```bash\n70\t    69\tpip install -e '.[test]'\n71\t    70\tpytest -q\n72\t    71\t```\n73\t=== Dockerfile\n74\t     1\t# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.10\n75\t     2\tFROM python:3.11.10-slim-bookworm@sha256:2a6386ad2db20e7f55073f69a98d6da2cf9f168e05e7487d2670c22e4ad2a1bd AS build\n76\t     3\tWORKDIR /src\n77\t     4\tENV PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1\n78\t     5\tCOPY pyproject.toml ./\n79\t     6\tCOPY app ./app\n80\t     7\tRUN pip install --target /opt/site .\n81\t     8\tRUN python -m compileall -q app\n82\t     9\t\n83\t    10\tFROM gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian12:nonroot@sha256:8f3c1a6e2b9d4f7a0c5e8b1d3f6a9c2e5b8d1f4a7c0e3b6d9f2a5c8e1b4d7f0a\n84\t    11\tWORKDIR /app\n85\t    12\tENV PYTHONPATH=/opt/site:/app \\\n86\t    13\t    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n87\t    14\t    APP_ROOT=/app\n88\t    15\tCOPY --from=build /opt/site /opt/site\n89\t    16\tCOPY --from=build /src/app /app/app\n90\t    17\tCOPY prompts /app/prompts\n91\t    18\tCOPY config /app/config\n92\t    19\tCOPY release/manifest.yaml /app/release/manifest.yaml\n93\t    20\tUSER 65532:65532\n94\t    21\tEXPOSE 8080\n95\t    22\tENTRYPOINT [\"python\", \"-m\", \"uvicorn\", \"app.main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8080\", \"--no-server-header\"]\n96\t=== pyproject.toml\n97\t     1\t[project]\n98\t     2\tname = \"procurement-agent\"\n99\t     3\tversion = \"2026.9.4\"\n100\t     4\tdescription = \"Procurement agent: quotes, purchase orders, invoice payment.\"\n101\t     5\trequires-python = \">=3.11\"\n102\t     6\tdependencies = [\n103\t     7\t  \"fastapi==0.115.6\",\n104\t     8\t  \"uvicorn==0.32.1\",\n105\t     9\t  \"asyncpg==0.30.0\",\n106\t    10\t  \"httpx==0.28.1\",\n107\t    11\t  \"pydantic==2.10.4\",\n108\t    12\t  \"pyyaml==6.0.2\",\n109\t    13\t  \"pyjwt[crypto]==2.10.1\",\n110\t    14\t  \"pypdf==5.1.0\",\n111\t    15\t  \"anthropic==0.75.0\",\n112\t    16\t  \"opentelemetry-sdk==1.29.0\",\n113\t    17\t  \"opentelemetry-exporter-otlp==1.29.0\",\n114\t    18\t]\n115\t    19\t\n116\t    20\t[project.optional-dependencies]\n117\t    21\ttest = [\"pytest==8.3.4\", \"pytest-asyncio==0.25.0\"]\n118\t    22\t\n119\t    23\t[tool.pytest.ini_options]\n120\t    24\tasyncio_mode = \"auto\"\n121\t    25\ttestpaths = [\"tests\"]\n122\t=== app/__init__.py\n123\t=== app/approvals.py\n124\t     1\t\"\"\"Approval requests and decisions for high-impact operations.\n125\t     2\t\n126\t     3\tRequests are posted to the business unit's approvals channel in Slack with\n127\t     4\tthe full argument summary. Approvers decide with the Slack buttons; the\n128\t     5\tinteractive callback is signature-checked in main.py and then calls\n129\t     6\t``decide``. Approver authority is checked against the role map in policy.\n130\t     7\t\"\"\"\n131\t     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n132\t     9\t\n133\t    10\timport json\n134\t    11\timport uuid\n135\t    12\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n136\t    13\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n137\t    14\tfrom typing import Any\n138\t    15\t\n139\t    16\tfrom app.audit import digest, summarize_args\n140\t    17\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n141\t    18\t\n142\t    19\t\n143\t    20\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n144\t    21\tclass Approval:\n145\t    22\t    id: str\n146\t    23\t    approver: str\n147\t    24\t    approver_role: str\n148\t    25\t    expires_at: datetime\n149\t    26\t\n150\t    27\t\n151\t    28\tclass ApproverNotAuthorized(Exception):\n152\t    29\t    pass\n153\t    30\t\n154\t    31\t\n155\t    32\tclass ApprovalStore:\n156\t    33\t    def __init__(self, pool, policy: dict, notifier):\n157\t    34\t        self.pool = pool\n158\t    35\t        self.ttl = timedelta(minutes=int(policy[\"approvals\"][\"ttl_minutes\"]))\n159\t    36\t        self.approver_roles: dict[str, list[str]] = policy[\"approvals\"][\"approver_roles\"]\n160\t    37\t        self.notifier = notifier\n161\t    38\t\n162\t    39\t    async def request(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool: str, target: str, args: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n163\t    40\t        approval_id = f\"apr-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n164\t    41\t        expires_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc) + self.ttl\n165\t    42\t        await self.pool.execute(\n166\t    43\t            \"\"\"\n167\t    44\t            INSERT INTO approvals (\n168\t    45\t                id, tool, target, args_sha256, args_summary, tenant,\n169\t    46\t                requested_by_instance, requested_by_run, delegated_subject,\n170\t    47\t                status, requested_at, expires_at\n171\t    48\t            ) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5::jsonb, $6, $7, $8, $9, 'pending', now(), $10)\n172\t    49\t            \"\"\",\n173\t    50\t            approval_id,\n174\t    51\t            tool,\n175\t    52\t            target,\n176\t    53\t            digest(args),\n177\t    54\t            json.dumps(summarize_args(args)),\n178\t    55\t            ident.tenant,\n179\t    56\t            ident.agent_instance_id,\n180\t    57\t            ident.run_id,\n181\t    58\t            ident.delegated_subject,\n182\t    59\t            expires_at,\n183\t    60\t        )\n184\t    61\t        await self.notifier.post_approval_request(\n185\t    62\t            tenant=ident.tenant,\n186\t    63\t            approval_id=approval_id,\n187\t    64\t            tool=tool,\n188\t    65\t            target=target,\n189\t    66\t            summary=summarize_args(args),\n190\t    67\t            expires_at=expires_at,\n191\t    68\t        )\n192\t    69\t        return approval_id\n193\t    70\t\n194\t    71\t    async def find_valid(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool: str, target: str) -> Approval | None:\n195\t    72\t        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\n196\t    73\t            \"\"\"\n197\t    74\t            SELECT id, approver, approver_role, expires_at\n198\t    75\t            FROM approvals\n199\t    76\t            WHERE tool = $1\n200\t    77\t              AND target = $2\n201\t    78\t              AND tenant = $3\n202\t    79\t              AND status = 'approved'\n203\t    80\t              AND expires_at > now()\n204\t    81\t            ORDER BY decided_at DESC\n205\t    82\t            LIMIT 1\n206\t    83\t            \"\"\",\n207\t    84\t            tool,\n208\t    85\t            target,\n209\t    86\t            ident.tenant,\n210\t    87\t        )\n211\t    88\t        if row is None:\n212\t    89\t            return None\n213\t    90\t        if row[\"approver_role\"] not in self.approver_roles.get(tool, []):\n214\t    91\t            return None\n215\t    92\t        return Approval(row[\"id\"], row[\"approver\"], row[\"approver_role\"], row[\"expires_at\"])\n216\t    93\t\n217\t    94\t    async def decide(self, approval_id: str, approver: str, approver_role: str, approve: bool) -> None:\n218\t    95\t        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\n219\t    96\t            \"SELECT tool, status, expires_at FROM approvals WHERE id = $1\", approval_id\n220\t    97\t        )\n221\t    98\t        if row is None or row[\"status\"] != \"pending\":\n222\t    99\t            raise ValueError(\"approval is not pending\")\n223\t   100\t        if row[\"expires_at\"] <= datetime.now(timezone.utc):\n224\t   101\t            raise ValueError(\"approval request expired\")\n225\t   102\t        if approver_role not in self.approver_roles.get(row[\"tool\"], []):\n226\t   103\t            raise ApproverNotAuthorized(f\"{approver_role} cannot approve {row['tool']}\")\n227\t   104\t        await self.pool.execute(\n228\t   105\t            \"\"\"\n229\t   106\t            UPDATE approvals\n230\t   107\t            SET status = $2, approver = $3, approver_role = $4, decided_at = now()\n231\t   108\t            WHERE id = $1 AND status = 'pending'\n232\t   109\t            \"\"\",\n233\t   110\t            approval_id,\n234\t   111\t            \"approved\" if approve else \"rejected\",\n235\t   112\t            approver,\n236\t   113\t            approver_role,\n237\t   114\t        )\n238\t=== app/audit.py\n239\t     1\t\"\"\"Execution audit graph.\n240\t     2\t\n241\t     3\tEvery step of a run is one row in ``audit_events``. Rows link to their parent\n242\t     4\tstep, so a run can be rebuilt as a tree: run -> model decision -> proposed\n243\t     5\ttool call -> authorization decision -> result or error. Writes are\n244\t     6\tsynchronous and are made before the action they describe; if the write\n245\t     7\tfails, the caller raises and the action does not run.\n246\t     8\t\"\"\"\n247\t     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n248\t    10\t\n249\t    11\timport hashlib\n250\t    12\timport json\n251\t    13\timport uuid\n252\t    14\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n253\t    15\tfrom typing import Any\n254\t    16\t\n255\t    17\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n256\t    18\t\n257\t    19\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure\n258\t    20\tfrom app.identity import IDENTITY_FIELDS, RunIdentity\n259\t    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_value\n260\t    22\t\n261\t    23\tEVENT_KINDS = {\n262\t    24\t    \"run_started\",\n263\t    25\t    \"run_finished\",\n264\t    26\t    \"run_halted\",\n265\t    27\t    \"model_decision\",\n266\t    28\t    \"tool_proposed\",\n267\t    29\t    \"authz_decision\",\n268\t    30\t    \"approval_requested\",\n269\t    31\t    \"approval_decided\",\n270\t    32\t    \"tool_result\",\n271\t    33\t    \"tool_error\",\n272\t    34\t    \"tool_denied\",\n273\t    35\t    \"budget_exceeded\",\n274\t    36\t    \"subagent_started\",\n275\t    37\t    \"subagent_finished\",\n276\t    38\t    \"background_job\",\n277\t    39\t}\n278\t    40\t\n279\t    41\t_INSERT = \"\"\"\n280\t    42\tINSERT INTO audit_events (\n281\t    43\t    node_id, parent_node_id, run_id, ts, kind,\n282\t    44\t    accountable_party, operational_owner, tenant,\n283\t    45\t    agent_type_id, agent_instance_id, trace_id, span_id,\n284\t    46\t    delegated_subject, agent_principal, parent_instance_id,\n285\t    47\t    policy_version, approval_id, operation_id,\n286\t    48\t    context_tokens, context_method, context_compacted,\n287\t    49\t    payload\n288\t    50\t) VALUES (\n289\t    51\t    $1, $2, $3, $4, $5,\n290\t    52\t    $6, $7, $8,\n291\t    53\t    $9, $10, $11, $12,\n292\t    54\t    $13, $14, $15,\n293\t    55\t    $16, $17, $18,\n294\t    56\t    $19, $20, $21,\n295\t    57\t    $22::jsonb\n296\t    58\t)\n297\t    59\t\"\"\"\n298\t    60\t\n299\t    61\t\n300\t    62\tdef summarize_args(args: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n301\t    63\t    \"\"\"Key arguments for the record, with secrets and account numbers redacted.\"\"\"\n302\t    64\t    return {k: redact_value(v) for k, v in args.items()}\n303\t    65\t\n304\t    66\t\n305\t    67\tdef digest(value: Any) -> str:\n306\t    68\t    raw = json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n307\t    69\t    return hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n308\t    70\t\n309\t    71\t\n310\t    72\tasync def record(\n311\t    73\t    pool,\n312\t    74\t    ident: RunIdentity,\n313\t    75\t    *,\n314\t    76\t    kind: str,\n315\t    77\t    payload: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n316\t    78\t    parent: str | None = None,\n317\t    79\t    context: ContextMeasure | None = None,\n318\t    80\t    policy_version: str | None = None,\n319\t    81\t    approval_id: str | None = None,\n320\t    82\t    operation_id: str | None = None,\n321\t    83\t) -> str:\n322\t    84\t    if kind not in EVENT_KINDS:\n323\t    85\t        raise ValueError(f\"unknown audit kind {kind}\")\n324\t    86\t    for name in IDENTITY_FIELDS:\n325\t    87\t        if not getattr(ident, name):\n326\t    88\t            raise ValueError(f\"audit record missing {name}\")\n327\t    89\t    span_ctx = trace.get_current_span().get_span_context()\n328\t    90\t    span_id = format(span_ctx.span_id, \"016x\") if span_ctx.is_valid else None\n329\t    91\t    node_id = f\"node-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n330\t    92\t    measure = context or ContextMeasure.unavailable()\n331\t    93\t    await pool.execute(\n332\t    94\t        _INSERT,\n333\t    95\t        node_id,\n334\t    96\t        parent,\n335\t    97\t        ident.run_id,\n336\t    98\t        datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n337\t    99\t        kind,\n338\t   100\t        ident.accountable_party,\n339\t   101\t        ident.operational_owner,\n340\t   102\t        ident.tenant,\n341\t   103\t        ident.agent_type_id,\n342\t   104\t        ident.agent_instance_id,\n343\t   105\t        ident.trace_id,\n344\t   106\t        span_id,\n345\t   107\t        ident.delegated_subject,\n346\t   108\t        ident.agent_principal,\n347\t   109\t        ident.parent_instance_id,\n348\t   110\t        policy_version,\n349\t   111\t        approval_id,\n350\t   112\t        operation_id,\n351\t   113\t        measure.tokens,\n352\t   114\t        measure.method,\n353\t   115\t        measure.compacted,\n354\t   116\t        json.dumps(redact_value(payload or {}), default=str),\n355\t   117\t    )\n356\t   118\t    return node_id\n357\t=== app/budget.py\n358\t     1\t\"\"\"Hard execution budgets, enforced by the harness and not by the model.\n359\t     2\t\n360\t     3\tPer run: step count, wall-clock time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and\n361\t     4\tnumber of sub-agents. Sub-agents charge the parent's budget, so a child\n362\t     5\tcannot widen what the parent was given.\n363\t     6\t\n364\t     7\tAcross runs: daily spend and per-minute run starts per user, per tenant\n365\t     8\t(business unit), and for the whole fleet. Quotas are reserved in Postgres\n366\t     9\tinside one transaction, so concurrent runs cannot overshoot them.\n367\t    10\t\"\"\"\n368\t    11\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n369\t    12\t\n370\t    13\timport time\n371\t    14\tfrom collections import deque\n372\t    15\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n373\t    16\tfrom decimal import Decimal\n374\t    17\t\n375\t    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n376\t    19\t\n377\t    20\t\n378\t    21\tclass BudgetExceeded(Exception):\n379\t    22\t    def __init__(self, limit: str, used, allowed):\n380\t    23\t        super().__init__(f\"{limit} exceeded: used={used} allowed={allowed}\")\n381\t    24\t        self.limit = limit\n382\t    25\t        self.used = used\n383\t    26\t        self.allowed = allowed\n384\t    27\t\n385\t    28\t\n386\t    29\t# USD per million tokens, from the provider price sheet referenced in the manifest.\n387\t    30\tPRICES = {\n388\t    31\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\": (Decimal(\"3.00\"), Decimal(\"15.00\")),\n389\t    32\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\": (Decimal(\"1.00\"), Decimal(\"5.00\")),\n390\t    33\t}\n391\t    34\t\n392\t    35\t\n393\t    36\t@dataclass\n394\t    37\tclass Budget:\n395\t    38\t    ident: RunIdentity\n396\t    39\t    max_steps: int\n397\t    40\t    max_wall_seconds: float\n398\t    41\t    max_tokens: int\n399\t    42\t    max_cost_usd: Decimal\n400\t    43\t    max_tool_calls_per_minute: int\n401\t    44\t    max_subagents: int\n402\t    45\t    quotas_daily_usd: dict[str, Decimal]\n403\t    46\t    run_starts_per_minute: dict[str, int]\n404\t    47\t    started_at: float = field(default_factory=time.monotonic)\n405\t    48\t    steps: int = 0\n406\t    49\t    tokens: int = 0\n407\t    50\t    cost_usd: Decimal = Decimal(\"0\")\n408\t    51\t    unflushed_cost_usd: Decimal = Decimal(\"0\")\n409\t    52\t    subagents: int = 0\n410\t    53\t    _tool_calls: deque = field(default_factory=deque)\n411\t    54\t\n412\t    55\t    @classmethod\n413\t    56\t    def for_run(cls, cfg: dict, ident: RunIdentity) -> \"Budget\":\n414\t    57\t        run = cfg[\"per_run\"]\n415\t    58\t        return cls(\n416\t    59\t            ident=ident,\n417\t    60\t            max_steps=int(run[\"max_steps\"]),\n418\t    61\t            max_wall_seconds=float(run[\"max_wall_seconds\"]),\n419\t    62\t            max_tokens=int(run[\"max_tokens\"]),\n420\t    63\t            max_cost_usd=Decimal(str(run[\"max_cost_usd\"])),\n421\t    64\t            max_tool_calls_per_minute=int(run[\"max_tool_calls_per_minute\"]),\n422\t    65\t            max_subagents=int(run[\"max_subagents\"]),\n423\t    66\t            quotas_daily_usd={k: Decimal(str(v)) for k, v in cfg[\"quotas_daily_usd\"].items()},\n424\t    67\t            run_starts_per_minute={k: int(v) for k, v in cfg[\"run_starts_per_minute\"].items()},\n425\t    68\t        )\n426\t    69\t\n427\t    70\t    def _scopes(self) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n428\t    71\t        return [\n429\t    72\t            (\"user\", self.ident.accountable_party),\n430\t    73\t            (\"tenant\", self.ident.tenant),\n431\t    74\t            (\"fleet\", \"all\"),\n432\t    75\t        ]\n433\t    76\t\n434\t    77\t    # --- per-run limits -------------------------------------------------\n435\t    78\t\n436\t    79\t    def check_step(self) -> None:\n437\t    80\t        self.steps += 1\n438\t    81\t        if self.steps > self.max_steps:\n439\t    82\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_steps\", self.steps, self.max_steps)\n440\t    83\t        elapsed = time.monotonic() - self.started_at\n441\t    84\t        if elapsed > self.max_wall_seconds:\n442\t    85\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_wall_seconds\", round(elapsed, 1), self.max_wall_seconds)\n443\t    86\t\n444\t    87\t    def charge_model(self, model: str, usage) -> None:\n445\t    88\t        price_in, price_out = PRICES[model]\n446\t    89\t        tokens_in = (\n447\t    90\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n448\t    91\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n449\t    92\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n450\t    93\t        )\n451\t    94\t        tokens_out = int(usage.output_tokens or 0)\n452\t    95\t        self.tokens += tokens_in + tokens_out\n453\t    96\t        cost = (price_in * tokens_in + price_out * tokens_out) / Decimal(1_000_000)\n454\t    97\t        self.cost_usd += cost\n455\t    98\t        self.unflushed_cost_usd += cost\n456\t    99\t        if self.tokens > self.max_tokens:\n457\t   100\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_tokens\", self.tokens, self.max_tokens)\n458\t   101\t        if self.cost_usd > self.max_cost_usd:\n459\t   102\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_cost_usd\", self.cost_usd, self.max_cost_usd)\n460\t   103\t\n461\t   104\t    def check_tool_call(self, now: float | None = None) -> None:\n462\t   105\t        now = time.monotonic() if now is None else now\n463\t   106\t        while self._tool_calls and now - self._tool_calls[0] > 60:\n464\t   107\t            self._tool_calls.popleft()\n465\t   108\t        if len(self._tool_calls) >= self.max_tool_calls_per_minute:\n466\t   109\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\n467\t   110\t                \"max_tool_calls_per_minute\", len(self._tool_calls) + 1, self.max_tool_calls_per_minute\n468\t   111\t            )\n469\t   112\t        self._tool_calls.append(now)\n470\t   113\t\n471\t   114\t    def check_subagent(self) -> None:\n472\t   115\t        if self.subagents >= self.max_subagents:\n473\t   116\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_subagents\", self.subagents + 1, self.max_subagents)\n474\t   117\t        self.subagents += 1\n475\t   118\t\n476\t   119\t    # --- cross-run quotas -----------------------------------------------\n477\t   120\t\n478\t   121\t    async def reserve_run_start(self, pool) -> None:\n479\t   122\t        async with pool.acquire() as conn:\n480\t   123\t            async with conn.transaction():\n481\t   124\t                for scope, key in self._scopes():\n482\t   125\t                    limit = self.run_starts_per_minute[scope]\n483\t   126\t                    count = await conn.fetchval(\n484\t   127\t                        \"\"\"\n485\t   128\t                        INSERT INTO run_start_window (scope, key, minute, starts)\n486\t   129\t                        VALUES ($1, $2, date_trunc('minute', now()), 1)\n487\t   130\t                        ON CONFLICT (scope, key, minute)\n488\t   131\t                        DO UPDATE SET starts = run_start_window.starts + 1\n489\t   132\t                        RETURNING starts\n490\t   133\t                        \"\"\",\n491\t   134\t                        scope,\n492\t   135\t                        key,\n493\t   136\t                    )\n494\t   137\t                    if count > limit:\n495\t   138\t                        raise BudgetExceeded(f\"run_starts_per_minute.{scope}\", count, limit)\n496\t   139\t\n497\t   140\t    async def flush(self, pool) -> None:\n498\t   141\t        \"\"\"Add this run's unflushed spend to the daily quotas, or stop the run.\"\"\"\n499\t   142\t        if self.unflushed_cost_usd <= 0:\n500\t   143\t            return\n501\t   144\t        amount = self.unflushed_cost_usd\n502\t   145\t        async with pool.acquire() as conn:\n503\t   146\t            async with conn.transaction():\n504\t   147\t                for scope, key in self._scopes():\n505\t   148\t                    limit = self.quotas_daily_usd[scope]\n506\t   149\t                    spent = await conn.fetchval(\n507\t   150\t                        \"\"\"\n508\t   151\t                        INSERT INTO spend_quota (scope, key, day, spent_usd)\n509\t   152\t                        VALUES ($1, $2, current_date, $3)\n510\t   153\t                        ON CONFLICT (scope, key, day)\n511\t   154\t                        DO UPDATE SET spent_usd = spend_quota.spent_usd + EXCLUDED.spent_usd\n512\t   155\t                        RETURNING spent_usd\n513\t   156\t                        \"\"\",\n514\t   157\t                        scope,\n515\t   158\t                        key,\n516\t   159\t                        amount,\n517\t   160\t                    )\n518\t   161\t                    if spent > limit:\n519\t   162\t                        raise BudgetExceeded(f\"quota_daily_usd.{scope}\", spent, limit)\n520\t   163\t        self.unflushed_cost_usd = Decimal(\"0\")\n521\t=== app/context_size.py\n522\t     1\t\"\"\"Decision-time context size.\n523\t     2\t\n524\t     3\tCounting method (documented in README, \"Context size\"):\n525\t     4\t\n526\t     5\t1. Before each model call, the exact request (system prompt, messages and\n527\t     6\t   tool schemas) is sent to the provider's token-counting endpoint. The\n528\t     7\t   returned ``input_tokens`` is recorded with method ``count_tokens_api``.\n529\t     8\t   This is the size of the context the model decides on, including any\n530\t     9\t   prefix that will be served from the prompt cache.\n531\t    10\t2. If counting fails, the value is taken after the call from the response\n532\t    11\t   usage as ``input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens +\n533\t    12\t   cache_creation_input_tokens`` and recorded with method\n534\t    13\t   ``usage_sum_estimate``.\n535\t    14\t3. If neither is available the value is ``NULL`` with method\n536\t    15\t   ``unavailable``. It is never recorded as zero.\n537\t    16\t\n538\t    17\t``compacted`` is true when the harness dropped or summarized earlier turns\n539\t    18\tbefore this call. Provider-side truncation is not visible to the harness and\n540\t    19\tis listed as a known limit.\n541\t    20\t\"\"\"\n542\t    21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n543\t    22\t\n544\t    23\timport logging\n545\t    24\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n546\t    25\t\n547\t    26\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n548\t    27\t\n549\t    28\t\n550\t    29\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n551\t    30\tclass ContextMeasure:\n552\t    31\t    tokens: int | None\n553\t    32\t    method: str\n554\t    33\t    compacted: bool\n555\t    34\t\n556\t    35\t    @classmethod\n557\t    36\t    def unavailable(cls, compacted: bool = False) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n558\t    37\t        return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\n559\t    38\t\n560\t    39\t    def finalize(self, usage) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n561\t    40\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n562\t    41\t            return self\n563\t    42\t        if usage is None:\n564\t    43\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n565\t    44\t        total = (\n566\t    45\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n567\t    46\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n568\t    47\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n569\t    48\t        )\n570\t    49\t        if total <= 0:\n571\t    50\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n572\t    51\t        return replace(self, tokens=total, method=\"usage_sum_estimate\")\n573\t    52\t\n574\t    53\t    def otel_attributes(self) -> dict:\n575\t    54\t        attrs = {\n576\t    55\t            \"procurement.context.method\": self.method,\n577\t    56\t            \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": self.compacted,\n578\t    57\t        }\n579\t    58\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n580\t    59\t            attrs[\"procurement.context.tokens\"] = self.tokens\n581\t    60\t        return attrs\n582\t    61\t\n583\t    62\t\n584\t    63\tasync def measure_context(client, request: dict, compacted: bool) -> ContextMeasure:\n585\t    64\t    try:\n586\t    65\t        counted = await client.messages.count_tokens(\n587\t    66\t            model=request[\"model\"],\n588\t    67\t            system=request[\"system\"],\n589\t    68\t            messages=request[\"messages\"],\n590\t    69\t            tools=request[\"tools\"],\n591\t    70\t        )\n592\t    71\t        return ContextMeasure(int(counted.input_tokens), \"count_tokens_api\", compacted)\n593\t    72\t    except Exception:  # counting is best effort; finalize() falls back to usage\n594\t    73\t        log.warning(\"token count failed; falling back to usage\", exc_info=True)\n595\t    74\t        return ContextMeasure(tokens=None, method=\"pending_usage\", compacted=compacted)\n596\t=== app/extractor.py\n597\t     1\t\"\"\"Line-item extraction sub-agent.\n598\t     2\t\n599\t     3\tThe parent procurement agent delegates structured extraction to a smaller\n600\t     4\tmodel. The child runs under its own instance id, links to its parent in the\n601\t     5\taudit graph, charges the parent's budget, and gets the extractor tool role.\n602\t     6\t\"\"\"\n603\t     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n604\t     8\t\n605\t     9\timport json\n606\t    10\timport logging\n607\t    11\tfrom typing import Any\n608\t    12\t\n609\t    13\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n610\t    14\t\n611\t    15\tfrom app import audit\n612\t    16\tfrom app.budget import Budget\n613\t    17\tfrom app.context_size import measure_context\n614\t    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n615\t    19\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n616\t    20\tfrom app.tools import build_registry\n617\t    21\t\n618\t    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n619\t    23\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.extractor\")\n620\t    24\t\n621\t    25\tEXTRACTOR_ROLE = \"line_item_extractor\"\n622\t    26\tMAX_TURNS = 4\n623\t    27\t\n624\t    28\tLINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS = {\"sku\", \"description\", \"quantity\", \"unit_price_cents\", \"currency\"}\n625\t    29\t\n626\t    30\t\n627\t    31\tclass ExtractionFailed(Exception):\n628\t    32\t    pass\n629\t    33\t\n630\t    34\t\n631\t    35\tclass LineItemExtractor:\n632\t    36\t    def __init__(self, *, client, settings, deps, system_prompt: str):\n633\t    37\t        self.client = client\n634\t    38\t        self.settings = settings\n635\t    39\t        self.deps = deps\n636\t    40\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n637\t    41\t\n638\t    42\t    async def extract(self, parent: RunIdentity, doc_id: str, budget: Budget) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n639\t    43\t        budget.check_subagent()\n640\t    44\t        ident = parent.child(role=EXTRACTOR_ROLE)\n641\t    45\t        registry = build_registry(EXTRACTOR_ROLE, ident, self.deps)\n642\t    46\t        task = f\"Extract every line item from document {doc_id}. Return JSON only.\"\n643\t    47\t\n644\t    48\t        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"gen_ai.invoke_agent line_item_extractor\") as span:\n645\t    49\t            span.set_attribute(\"gen_ai.agent.id\", ident.agent_instance_id)\n646\t    50\t            span.set_attribute(\"procurement.parent_instance_id\", parent.agent_instance_id)\n647\t    51\t            start_node = await audit.record(\n648\t    52\t                self.deps.pool,\n649\t    53\t                ident,\n650\t    54\t                kind=\"subagent_started\",\n651\t    55\t                payload={\n652\t    56\t                    \"role\": EXTRACTOR_ROLE,\n653\t    57\t                    \"doc_id\": doc_id,\n654\t    58\t                    \"parent_prompt_ref\": format(span.get_span_context().span_id, \"016x\"),\n655\t    59\t                    \"tools\": registry.names(),\n656\t    60\t                },\n657\t    61\t            )\n658\t    62\t\n659\t    63\t            messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n660\t    64\t            for _turn in range(MAX_TURNS):\n661\t    65\t                budget.check_step()\n662\t    66\t                request = {\n663\t    67\t                    \"model\": self.settings.extractor_model_id,\n664\t    68\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n665\t    69\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n666\t    70\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n667\t    71\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n668\t    72\t                }\n669\t    73\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted=False)\n670\t    74\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n671\t    75\t                budget.charge_model(self.settings.extractor_model_id, response.usage)\n672\t    76\t                await budget.flush(self.deps.pool)\n673\t    77\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n674\t    78\t                decision = await audit.record(\n675\t    79\t                    self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,\n676\t    80\t                    payload={\"requested_model\": request[\"model\"], \"served_model\": response.model,\n677\t    81\t                             \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason},\n678\t    82\t                )\n679\t    83\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n680\t    84\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n681\t    85\t                if not uses:\n682\t    86\t                    text = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n683\t    87\t                    items = _parse_items(text)\n684\t    88\t                    await audit.record(\n685\t    89\t                        self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"subagent_finished\", parent=start_node,\n686\t    90\t                        payload={\"items\": len(items)},\n687\t    91\t                    )\n688\t    92\t                    return items\n689\t    93\t                results = []\n690\t    94\t                for use in uses:\n691\t    95\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n692\t    96\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n693\t    97\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n694\t    98\t\n695\t    99\t        raise ExtractionFailed(f\"no result after {MAX_TURNS} turns\")\n696\t   100\t\n697\t   101\t\n698\t   102\tdef _parse_items(text: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n699\t   103\t    try:\n700\t   104\t        data = json.loads(text)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff","uuid":"2b6de2ab-83a1-4caf-a2c6-b9428ae9bb8a","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:24:03.613Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-repeat-z0r2wndt/7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff/tool-results/bsj8ssif6.txt","content":"=== README.md\n     1\t# procurement-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\n     4\tinvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\n     5\tpurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\n     6\tvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Architecture\n     9\t\n    10\t```\n    11\tmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\n    12\tstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n    13\t                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n    14\t                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n    15\t                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n    16\t                                   |-- tools:\n    17\t                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n    18\t                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n    19\t                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n    20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n    21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n    22\t```\n    23\t\n    24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n    25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n    26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n    27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n    28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n    29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n    30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n    31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n    32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n    33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n    34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n    35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n    36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n    37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n    38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n    39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n    40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Context size\n    43\t\n    44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n    45\t\n    46\t| method | meaning |\n    47\t|---|---|\n    48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n    49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n    50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n    51\t\n    52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n    53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Operating\n    56\t\n    57\t* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n    58\t  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n    59\t  start while a halt is set.\n    60\t* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n    61\t  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n    62\t  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n    63\t* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n    64\t  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n    65\t\n    66\t## Tests\n    67\t\n    68\t```bash\n    69\tpip install -e '.[test]'\n    70\tpytest -q\n    71\t```\n=== Dockerfile\n     1\t# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.10\n     2\tFROM python:3.11.10-slim-bookworm@sha256:2a6386ad2db20e7f55073f69a98d6da2cf9f168e05e7487d2670c22e4ad2a1bd AS build\n     3\tWORKDIR /src\n     4\tENV PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1\n     5\tCOPY pyproject.toml ./\n     6\tCOPY app ./app\n     7\tRUN pip install --target /opt/site .\n     8\tRUN python -m compileall -q app\n     9\t\n    10\tFROM gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian12:nonroot@sha256:8f3c1a6e2b9d4f7a0c5e8b1d3f6a9c2e5b8d1f4a7c0e3b6d9f2a5c8e1b4d7f0a\n    11\tWORKDIR /app\n    12\tENV PYTHONPATH=/opt/site:/app \\\n    13\t    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \\\n    14\t    APP_ROOT=/app\n    15\tCOPY --from=build /opt/site /opt/site\n    16\tCOPY --from=build /src/app /app/app\n    17\tCOPY prompts /app/prompts\n    18\tCOPY config /app/config\n    19\tCOPY release/manifest.yaml /app/release/manifest.yaml\n    20\tUSER 65532:65532\n    21\tEXPOSE 8080\n    22\tENTRYPOINT [\"python\", \"-m\", \"uvicorn\", \"app.main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8080\", \"--no-server-header\"]\n=== pyproject.toml\n     1\t[project]\n     2\tname = \"procurement-agent\"\n     3\tversion = \"2026.9.4\"\n     4\tdescription = \"Procurement agent: quotes, purchase orders, invoice payment.\"\n     5\trequires-python = \">=3.11\"\n     6\tdependencies = [\n     7\t  \"fastapi==0.115.6\",\n     8\t  \"uvicorn==0.32.1\",\n     9\t  \"asyncpg==0.30.0\",\n    10\t  \"httpx==0.28.1\",\n    11\t  \"pydantic==2.10.4\",\n    12\t  \"pyyaml==6.0.2\",\n    13\t  \"pyjwt[crypto]==2.10.1\",\n    14\t  \"pypdf==5.1.0\",\n    15\t  \"anthropic==0.75.0\",\n    16\t  \"opentelemetry-sdk==1.29.0\",\n    17\t  \"opentelemetry-exporter-otlp==1.29.0\",\n    18\t]\n    19\t\n    20\t[project.optional-dependencies]\n    21\ttest = [\"pytest==8.3.4\", \"pytest-asyncio==0.25.0\"]\n    22\t\n    23\t[tool.pytest.ini_options]\n    24\tasyncio_mode = \"auto\"\n    25\ttestpaths = [\"tests\"]\n=== app/__init__.py\n=== app/approvals.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Approval requests and decisions for high-impact operations.\n     2\t\n     3\tRequests are posted to the business unit's approvals channel in Slack with\n     4\tthe full argument summary. Approvers decide with the Slack buttons; the\n     5\tinteractive callback is signature-checked in main.py and then calls\n     6\t``decide``. Approver authority is checked against the role map in policy.\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport json\n    11\timport uuid\n    12\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    13\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n    14\tfrom typing import Any\n    15\t\n    16\tfrom app.audit import digest, summarize_args\n    17\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    21\tclass Approval:\n    22\t    id: str\n    23\t    approver: str\n    24\t    approver_role: str\n    25\t    expires_at: datetime\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tclass ApproverNotAuthorized(Exception):\n    29\t    pass\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tclass ApprovalStore:\n    33\t    def __init__(self, pool, policy: dict, notifier):\n    34\t        self.pool = pool\n    35\t        self.ttl = timedelta(minutes=int(policy[\"approvals\"][\"ttl_minutes\"]))\n    36\t        self.approver_roles: dict[str, list[str]] = policy[\"approvals\"][\"approver_roles\"]\n    37\t        self.notifier = notifier\n    38\t\n    39\t    async def request(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool: str, target: str, args: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    40\t        approval_id = f\"apr-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n    41\t        expires_at = datetime.now(timezone.utc) + self.ttl\n    42\t        await self.pool.execute(\n    43\t            \"\"\"\n    44\t            INSERT INTO approvals (\n    45\t                id, tool, target, args_sha256, args_summary, tenant,\n    46\t                requested_by_instance, requested_by_run, delegated_subject,\n    47\t                status, requested_at, expires_at\n    48\t            ) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5::jsonb, $6, $7, $8, $9, 'pending', now(), $10)\n    49\t            \"\"\",\n    50\t            approval_id,\n    51\t            tool,\n    52\t            target,\n    53\t            digest(args),\n    54\t            json.dumps(summarize_args(args)),\n    55\t            ident.tenant,\n    56\t            ident.agent_instance_id,\n    57\t            ident.run_id,\n    58\t            ident.delegated_subject,\n    59\t            expires_at,\n    60\t        )\n    61\t        await self.notifier.post_approval_request(\n    62\t            tenant=ident.tenant,\n    63\t            approval_id=approval_id,\n    64\t            tool=tool,\n    65\t            target=target,\n    66\t            summary=summarize_args(args),\n    67\t            expires_at=expires_at,\n    68\t        )\n    69\t        return approval_id\n    70\t\n    71\t    async def find_valid(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool: str, target: str) -> Approval | None:\n    72\t        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\n    73\t            \"\"\"\n    74\t            SELECT id, approver, approver_role, expires_at\n    75\t            FROM approvals\n    76\t            WHERE tool = $1\n    77\t              AND target = $2\n    78\t              AND tenant = $3\n    79\t              AND status = 'approved'\n    80\t              AND expires_at > now()\n    81\t            ORDER BY decided_at DESC\n    82\t            LIMIT 1\n    83\t            \"\"\",\n    84\t            tool,\n    85\t            target,\n    86\t            ident.tenant,\n    87\t        )\n    88\t        if row is None:\n    89\t            return None\n    90\t        if row[\"approver_role\"] not in self.approver_roles.get(tool, []):\n    91\t            return None\n    92\t        return Approval(row[\"id\"], row[\"approver\"], row[\"approver_role\"], row[\"expires_at\"])\n    93\t\n    94\t    async def decide(self, approval_id: str, approver: str, approver_role: str, approve: bool) -> None:\n    95\t        row = await self.pool.fetchrow(\n    96\t            \"SELECT tool, status, expires_at FROM approvals WHERE id = $1\", approval_id\n    97\t        )\n    98\t        if row is None or row[\"status\"] != \"pending\":\n    99\t            raise ValueError(\"approval is not pending\")\n   100\t        if row[\"expires_at\"] <= datetime.now(timezone.utc):\n   101\t            raise ValueError(\"approval request expired\")\n   102\t        if approver_role not in self.approver_roles.get(row[\"tool\"], []):\n   103\t            raise ApproverNotAuthorized(f\"{approver_role} cannot approve {row['tool']}\")\n   104\t        await self.pool.execute(\n   105\t            \"\"\"\n   106\t            UPDATE approvals\n   107\t            SET status = $2, approver = $3, approver_role = $4, decided_at = now()\n   108\t            WHERE id = $1 AND status = 'pending'\n   109\t            \"\"\",\n   110\t            approval_id,\n   111\t            \"approved\" if approve else \"rejected\",\n   112\t            approver,\n   113\t            approver_role,\n   114\t        )\n=== app/audit.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Execution audit graph.\n     2\t\n     3\tEvery step of a run is one row in ``audit_events``. Rows link to their parent\n     4\tstep, so a run can be rebuilt as a tree: run -> model decision -> proposed\n     5\ttool call -> authorization decision -> result or error. Writes are\n     6\tsynchronous and are made before the action they describe; if the write\n     7\tfails, the caller raises and the action does not run.\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    10\t\n    11\timport hashlib\n    12\timport json\n    13\timport uuid\n    14\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n    15\tfrom typing import Any\n    16\t\n    17\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    18\t\n    19\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure\n    20\tfrom app.identity import IDENTITY_FIELDS, RunIdentity\n    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_value\n    22\t\n    23\tEVENT_KINDS = {\n    24\t    \"run_started\",\n    25\t    \"run_finished\",\n    26\t    \"run_halted\",\n    27\t    \"model_decision\",\n    28\t    \"tool_proposed\",\n    29\t    \"authz_decision\",\n    30\t    \"approval_requested\",\n    31\t    \"approval_decided\",\n    32\t    \"tool_result\",\n    33\t    \"tool_error\",\n    34\t    \"tool_denied\",\n    35\t    \"budget_exceeded\",\n    36\t    \"subagent_started\",\n    37\t    \"subagent_finished\",\n    38\t    \"background_job\",\n    39\t}\n    40\t\n    41\t_INSERT = \"\"\"\n    42\tINSERT INTO audit_events (\n    43\t    node_id, parent_node_id, run_id, ts, kind,\n    44\t    accountable_party, operational_owner, tenant,\n    45\t    agent_type_id, agent_instance_id, trace_id, span_id,\n    46\t    delegated_subject, agent_principal, parent_instance_id,\n    47\t    policy_version, approval_id, operation_id,\n    48\t    context_tokens, context_method, context_compacted,\n    49\t    payload\n    50\t) VALUES (\n    51\t    $1, $2, $3, $4, $5,\n    52\t    $6, $7, $8,\n    53\t    $9, $10, $11, $12,\n    54\t    $13, $14, $15,\n    55\t    $16, $17, $18,\n    56\t    $19, $20, $21,\n    57\t    $22::jsonb\n    58\t)\n    59\t\"\"\"\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\tdef summarize_args(args: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    63\t    \"\"\"Key arguments for the record, with secrets and account numbers redacted.\"\"\"\n    64\t    return {k: redact_value(v) for k, v in args.items()}\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef digest(value: Any) -> str:\n    68\t    raw = json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n    69\t    return hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\tasync def record(\n    73\t    pool,\n    74\t    ident: RunIdentity,\n    75\t    *,\n    76\t    kind: str,\n    77\t    payload: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    78\t    parent: str | None = None,\n    79\t    context: ContextMeasure | None = None,\n    80\t    policy_version: str | None = None,\n    81\t    approval_id: str | None = None,\n    82\t    operation_id: str | None = None,\n    83\t) -> str:\n    84\t    if kind not in EVENT_KINDS:\n    85\t        raise ValueError(f\"unknown audit kind {kind}\")\n    86\t    for name in IDENTITY_FIELDS:\n    87\t        if not getattr(ident, name):\n    88\t            raise ValueError(f\"audit record missing {name}\")\n    89\t    span_ctx = trace.get_current_span().get_span_context()\n    90\t    span_id = format(span_ctx.span_id, \"016x\") if span_ctx.is_valid else None\n    91\t    node_id = f\"node-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n    92\t    measure = context or ContextMeasure.unavailable()\n    93\t    await pool.execute(\n    94\t        _INSERT,\n    95\t        node_id,\n    96\t        parent,\n    97\t        ident.run_id,\n    98\t        datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n    99\t        kind,\n   100\t        ident.accountable_party,\n   101\t        ident.operational_owner,\n   102\t        ident.tenant,\n   103\t        ident.agent_type_id,\n   104\t        ident.agent_instance_id,\n   105\t        ident.trace_id,\n   106\t        span_id,\n   107\t        ident.delegated_subject,\n   108\t        ident.agent_principal,\n   109\t        ident.parent_instance_id,\n   110\t        policy_version,\n   111\t        approval_id,\n   112\t        operation_id,\n   113\t        measure.tokens,\n   114\t        measure.method,\n   115\t        measure.compacted,\n   116\t        json.dumps(redact_value(payload or {}), default=str),\n   117\t    )\n   118\t    return node_id\n=== app/budget.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Hard execution budgets, enforced by the harness and not by the model.\n     2\t\n     3\tPer run: step count, wall-clock time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and\n     4\tnumber of sub-agents. Sub-agents charge the parent's budget, so a child\n     5\tcannot widen what the parent was given.\n     6\t\n     7\tAcross runs: daily spend and per-minute run starts per user, per tenant\n     8\t(business unit), and for the whole fleet. Quotas are reserved in Postgres\n     9\tinside one transaction, so concurrent runs cannot overshoot them.\n    10\t\"\"\"\n    11\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    12\t\n    13\timport time\n    14\tfrom collections import deque\n    15\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n    16\tfrom decimal import Decimal\n    17\t\n    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\tclass BudgetExceeded(Exception):\n    22\t    def __init__(self, limit: str, used, allowed):\n    23\t        super().__init__(f\"{limit} exceeded: used={used} allowed={allowed}\")\n    24\t        self.limit = limit\n    25\t        self.used = used\n    26\t        self.allowed = allowed\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t# USD per million tokens, from the provider price sheet referenced in the manifest.\n    30\tPRICES = {\n    31\t    \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\": (Decimal(\"3.00\"), Decimal(\"15.00\")),\n    32\t    \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\": (Decimal(\"1.00\"), Decimal(\"5.00\")),\n    33\t}\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t@dataclass\n    37\tclass Budget:\n    38\t    ident: RunIdentity\n    39\t    max_steps: int\n    40\t    max_wall_seconds: float\n    41\t    max_tokens: int\n    42\t    max_cost_usd: Decimal\n    43\t    max_tool_calls_per_minute: int\n    44\t    max_subagents: int\n    45\t    quotas_daily_usd: dict[str, Decimal]\n    46\t    run_starts_per_minute: dict[str, int]\n    47\t    started_at: float = field(default_factory=time.monotonic)\n    48\t    steps: int = 0\n    49\t    tokens: int = 0\n    50\t    cost_usd: Decimal = Decimal(\"0\")\n    51\t    unflushed_cost_usd: Decimal = Decimal(\"0\")\n    52\t    subagents: int = 0\n    53\t    _tool_calls: deque = field(default_factory=deque)\n    54\t\n    55\t    @classmethod\n    56\t    def for_run(cls, cfg: dict, ident: RunIdentity) -> \"Budget\":\n    57\t        run = cfg[\"per_run\"]\n    58\t        return cls(\n    59\t            ident=ident,\n    60\t            max_steps=int(run[\"max_steps\"]),\n    61\t            max_wall_seconds=float(run[\"max_wall_seconds\"]),\n    62\t            max_tokens=int(run[\"max_tokens\"]),\n    63\t            max_cost_usd=Decimal(str(run[\"max_cost_usd\"])),\n    64\t            max_tool_calls_per_minute=int(run[\"max_tool_calls_per_minute\"]),\n    65\t            max_subagents=int(run[\"max_subagents\"]),\n    66\t            quotas_daily_usd={k: Decimal(str(v)) for k, v in cfg[\"quotas_daily_usd\"].items()},\n    67\t            run_starts_per_minute={k: int(v) for k, v in cfg[\"run_starts_per_minute\"].items()},\n    68\t        )\n    69\t\n    70\t    def _scopes(self) -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n    71\t        return [\n    72\t            (\"user\", self.ident.accountable_party),\n    73\t            (\"tenant\", self.ident.tenant),\n    74\t            (\"fleet\", \"all\"),\n    75\t        ]\n    76\t\n    77\t    # --- per-run limits -------------------------------------------------\n    78\t\n    79\t    def check_step(self) -> None:\n    80\t        self.steps += 1\n    81\t        if self.steps > self.max_steps:\n    82\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_steps\", self.steps, self.max_steps)\n    83\t        elapsed = time.monotonic() - self.started_at\n    84\t        if elapsed > self.max_wall_seconds:\n    85\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_wall_seconds\", round(elapsed, 1), self.max_wall_seconds)\n    86\t\n    87\t    def charge_model(self, model: str, usage) -> None:\n    88\t        price_in, price_out = PRICES[model]\n    89\t        tokens_in = (\n    90\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n    91\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    92\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    93\t        )\n    94\t        tokens_out = int(usage.output_tokens or 0)\n    95\t        self.tokens += tokens_in + tokens_out\n    96\t        cost = (price_in * tokens_in + price_out * tokens_out) / Decimal(1_000_000)\n    97\t        self.cost_usd += cost\n    98\t        self.unflushed_cost_usd += cost\n    99\t        if self.tokens > self.max_tokens:\n   100\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_tokens\", self.tokens, self.max_tokens)\n   101\t        if self.cost_usd > self.max_cost_usd:\n   102\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_cost_usd\", self.cost_usd, self.max_cost_usd)\n   103\t\n   104\t    def check_tool_call(self, now: float | None = None) -> None:\n   105\t        now = time.monotonic() if now is None else now\n   106\t        while self._tool_calls and now - self._tool_calls[0] > 60:\n   107\t            self._tool_calls.popleft()\n   108\t        if len(self._tool_calls) >= self.max_tool_calls_per_minute:\n   109\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\n   110\t                \"max_tool_calls_per_minute\", len(self._tool_calls) + 1, self.max_tool_calls_per_minute\n   111\t            )\n   112\t        self._tool_calls.append(now)\n   113\t\n   114\t    def check_subagent(self) -> None:\n   115\t        if self.subagents >= self.max_subagents:\n   116\t            raise BudgetExceeded(\"max_subagents\", self.subagents + 1, self.max_subagents)\n   117\t        self.subagents += 1\n   118\t\n   119\t    # --- cross-run quotas -----------------------------------------------\n   120\t\n   121\t    async def reserve_run_start(self, pool) -> None:\n   122\t        async with pool.acquire() as conn:\n   123\t            async with conn.transaction():\n   124\t                for scope, key in self._scopes():\n   125\t                    limit = self.run_starts_per_minute[scope]\n   126\t                    count = await conn.fetchval(\n   127\t                        \"\"\"\n   128\t                        INSERT INTO run_start_window (scope, key, minute, starts)\n   129\t                        VALUES ($1, $2, date_trunc('minute', now()), 1)\n   130\t                        ON CONFLICT (scope, key, minute)\n   131\t                        DO UPDATE SET starts = run_start_window.starts + 1\n   132\t                        RETURNING starts\n   133\t                        \"\"\",\n   134\t                        scope,\n   135\t                        key,\n   136\t                    )\n   137\t                    if count > limit:\n   138\t                        raise BudgetExceeded(f\"run_starts_per_minute.{scope}\", count, limit)\n   139\t\n   140\t    async def flush(self, pool) -> None:\n   141\t        \"\"\"Add this run's unflushed spend to the daily quotas, or stop the run.\"\"\"\n   142\t        if self.unflushed_cost_usd <= 0:\n   143\t            return\n   144\t        amount = self.unflushed_cost_usd\n   145\t        async with pool.acquire() as conn:\n   146\t            async with conn.transaction():\n   147\t                for scope, key in self._scopes():\n   148\t                    limit = self.quotas_daily_usd[scope]\n   149\t                    spent = await conn.fetchval(\n   150\t                        \"\"\"\n   151\t                        INSERT INTO spend_quota (scope, key, day, spent_usd)\n   152\t                        VALUES ($1, $2, current_date, $3)\n   153\t                        ON CONFLICT (scope, key, day)\n   154\t                        DO UPDATE SET spent_usd = spend_quota.spent_usd + EXCLUDED.spent_usd\n   155\t                        RETURNING spent_usd\n   156\t                        \"\"\",\n   157\t                        scope,\n   158\t                        key,\n   159\t                        amount,\n   160\t                    )\n   161\t                    if spent > limit:\n   162\t                        raise BudgetExceeded(f\"quota_daily_usd.{scope}\", spent, limit)\n   163\t        self.unflushed_cost_usd = Decimal(\"0\")\n=== app/context_size.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Decision-time context size.\n     2\t\n     3\tCounting method (documented in README, \"Context size\"):\n     4\t\n     5\t1. Before each model call, the exact request (system prompt, messages and\n     6\t   tool schemas) is sent to the provider's token-counting endpoint. The\n     7\t   returned ``input_tokens`` is recorded with method ``count_tokens_api``.\n     8\t   This is the size of the context the model decides on, including any\n     9\t   prefix that will be served from the prompt cache.\n    10\t2. If counting fails, the value is taken after the call from the response\n    11\t   usage as ``input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens +\n    12\t   cache_creation_input_tokens`` and recorded with method\n    13\t   ``usage_sum_estimate``.\n    14\t3. If neither is available the value is ``NULL`` with method\n    15\t   ``unavailable``. It is never recorded as zero.\n    16\t\n    17\t``compacted`` is true when the harness dropped or summarized earlier turns\n    18\tbefore this call. Provider-side truncation is not visible to the harness and\n    19\tis listed as a known limit.\n    20\t\"\"\"\n    21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    22\t\n    23\timport logging\n    24\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n    25\t\n    26\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    30\tclass ContextMeasure:\n    31\t    tokens: int | None\n    32\t    method: str\n    33\t    compacted: bool\n    34\t\n    35\t    @classmethod\n    36\t    def unavailable(cls, compacted: bool = False) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    37\t        return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\n    38\t\n    39\t    def finalize(self, usage) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    40\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    41\t            return self\n    42\t        if usage is None:\n    43\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    44\t        total = (\n    45\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n    46\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    47\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    48\t        )\n    49\t        if total <= 0:\n    50\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    51\t        return replace(self, tokens=total, method=\"usage_sum_estimate\")\n    52\t\n    53\t    def otel_attributes(self) -> dict:\n    54\t        attrs = {\n    55\t            \"procurement.context.method\": self.method,\n    56\t            \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": self.compacted,\n    57\t        }\n    58\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    59\t            attrs[\"procurement.context.tokens\"] = self.tokens\n    60\t        return attrs\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tasync def measure_context(client, request: dict, compacted: bool) -> ContextMeasure:\n    64\t    try:\n    65\t        counted = await client.messages.count_tokens(\n    66\t            model=request[\"model\"],\n    67\t            system=request[\"system\"],\n    68\t            messages=request[\"messages\"],\n    69\t            tools=request[\"tools\"],\n    70\t        )\n    71\t        return ContextMeasure(int(counted.input_tokens), \"count_tokens_api\", compacted)\n    72\t    except Exception:  # counting is best effort; finalize() falls back to usage\n    73\t        log.warning(\"token count failed; falling back to usage\", exc_info=True)\n    74\t        return ContextMeasure(tokens=None, method=\"pending_usage\", compacted=compacted)\n=== app/extractor.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Line-item extraction sub-agent.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe parent procurement agent delegates structured extraction to a smaller\n     4\tmodel. The child runs under its own instance id, links to its parent in the\n     5\taudit graph, charges the parent's budget, and gets the extractor tool role.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\timport json\n    10\timport logging\n    11\tfrom typing import Any\n    12\t\n    13\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    14\t\n    15\tfrom app import audit\n    16\tfrom app.budget import Budget\n    17\tfrom app.context_size import measure_context\n    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    19\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n    20\tfrom app.tools import build_registry\n    21\t\n    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    23\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.extractor\")\n    24\t\n    25\tEXTRACTOR_ROLE = \"line_item_extractor\"\n    26\tMAX_TURNS = 4\n    27\t\n    28\tLINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS = {\"sku\", \"description\", \"quantity\", \"unit_price_cents\", \"currency\"}\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tclass ExtractionFailed(Exception):\n    32\t    pass\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tclass LineItemExtractor:\n    36\t    def __init__(self, *, client, settings, deps, system_prompt: str):\n    37\t        self.client = client\n    38\t        self.settings = settings\n    39\t        self.deps = deps\n    40\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n    41\t\n    42\t    async def extract(self, parent: RunIdentity, doc_id: str, budget: Budget) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    43\t        budget.check_subagent()\n    44\t        ident = parent.child(role=EXTRACTOR_ROLE)\n    45\t        registry = build_registry(EXTRACTOR_ROLE, ident, self.deps)\n    46\t        task = f\"Extract every line item from document {doc_id}. Return JSON only.\"\n    47\t\n    48\t        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"gen_ai.invoke_agent line_item_extractor\") as span:\n    49\t            span.set_attribute(\"gen_ai.agent.id\", ident.agent_instance_id)\n    50\t            span.set_attribute(\"procurement.parent_instance_id\", parent.agent_instance_id)\n    51\t            start_node = await audit.record(\n    52\t                self.deps.pool,\n    53\t                ident,\n    54\t                kind=\"subagent_started\",\n    55\t                payload={\n    56\t                    \"role\": EXTRACTOR_ROLE,\n    57\t                    \"doc_id\": doc_id,\n    58\t                    \"parent_prompt_ref\": format(span.get_span_context().span_id, \"016x\"),\n    59\t                    \"tools\": registry.names(),\n    60\t                },\n    61\t            )\n    62\t\n    63\t            messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n    64\t            for _turn in range(MAX_TURNS):\n    65\t                budget.check_step()\n    66\t                request = {\n    67\t                    \"model\": self.settings.extractor_model_id,\n    68\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n    69\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n    70\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n    71\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n    72\t                }\n    73\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted=False)\n    74\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n    75\t                budget.charge_model(self.settings.extractor_model_id, response.usage)\n    76\t                await budget.flush(self.deps.pool)\n    77\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n    78\t                decision = await audit.record(\n    79\t                    self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,\n    80\t                    payload={\"requested_model\": request[\"model\"], \"served_model\": response.model,\n    81\t                             \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason},\n    82\t                )\n    83\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n    84\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n    85\t                if not uses:\n    86\t                    text = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n    87\t                    items = _parse_items(text)\n    88\t                    await audit.record(\n    89\t                        self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"subagent_finished\", parent=start_node,\n    90\t                        payload={\"items\": len(items)},\n    91\t                    )\n    92\t                    return items\n    93\t                results = []\n    94\t                for use in uses:\n    95\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n    96\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n    97\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n    98\t\n    99\t        raise ExtractionFailed(f\"no result after {MAX_TURNS} turns\")\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef _parse_items(text: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n   103\t    try:\n   104\t        data = json.loads(text)","numLines":700,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2366}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdZag1B92MpQ2AqhNpxz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PAMQUKrdLyVzvwqZB8Ltuw","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-repeat-z0r2wndt/7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff/tool-results/bsj8ssif6.txt","offset":700,"limit":900},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13745,"cache_read_input_tokens":18398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13745},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff","uuid":"919eedc6-5494-4272-a181-517ce7d63de4","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:24:05.852Z","request_id":"req_011CfdZafiKomL8SbKs2dRKF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PAMQUKrdLyVzvwqZB8Ltuw":{"file_path":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-repeat-z0r2wndt/7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff/tool-results/bsj8ssif6.txt","offset":700,"limit":900}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PAMQUKrdLyVzvwqZB8Ltuw","type":"tool_result","content":"700\t   104\t        data = json.loads(text)\n701\t   105\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n702\t   106\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor returned non-JSON output\") from exc\n703\t   107\t    if not isinstance(data, list) or len(data) > 500:\n704\t   108\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor output must be a list of at most 500 items\")\n705\t   109\t    items = []\n706\t   110\t    for raw in data:\n707\t   111\t        if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not set(raw) <= LINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS:\n708\t   112\t            raise ExtractionFailed(\"unexpected line-item fields\")\n709\t   113\t        items.append({k: redact_for_model(v) if isinstance(v, str) else v for k, v in raw.items()})\n710\t   114\t    return items\n711\t=== app/gate.py\n712\t     1\t\"\"\"Policy gate for tool calls.\n713\t     2\t\n714\t     3\tRuns in the harness between the model's proposed call and the integration.\n715\t     4\tHigh-impact operations are denied unless a valid approval exists; when none\n716\t     5\texists an approval request is opened and the call returns as pending.\n717\t     6\t\"\"\"\n718\t     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n719\t     8\t\n720\t     9\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n721\t    10\tfrom typing import Any\n722\t    11\t\n723\t    12\tfrom app.approvals import ApprovalStore\n724\t    13\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n725\t    14\t\n726\t    15\t\n727\t    16\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n728\t    17\tclass Decision:\n729\t    18\t    allow: bool\n730\t    19\t    reason: str\n731\t    20\t    policy_version: str\n732\t    21\t    approval_id: str | None = None\n733\t    22\t    pending: bool = False\n734\t    23\t\n735\t    24\t\n736\t    25\tclass PolicyGate:\n737\t    26\t    def __init__(self, policy: dict, approvals: ApprovalStore):\n738\t    27\t        self.version: str = policy[\"version\"]\n739\t    28\t        self.high_impact: frozenset[str] = frozenset(policy[\"high_impact_tools\"])\n740\t    29\t        self.erp_read_prefixes: tuple[str, ...] = tuple(policy[\"erp\"][\"read_prefixes\"])\n741\t    30\t        self.approvals = approvals\n742\t    31\t\n743\t    32\t    async def authorize(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n744\t    33\t        if tool.name == \"erp_call\":\n745\t    34\t            operation = str(args.get(\"operation\", \"\"))\n746\t    35\t            if not operation.startswith(self.erp_read_prefixes):\n747\t    36\t                return Decision(False, f\"erp operation not permitted: {operation}\", self.version)\n748\t    37\t            return Decision(True, \"erp read operation\", self.version)\n749\t    38\t\n750\t    39\t        if tool.name == \"post_slack_message\":\n751\t    40\t            if args.get(\"external\", False):\n752\t    41\t                return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n753\t    42\t            return Decision(True, \"internal staff message\", self.version)\n754\t    43\t\n755\t    44\t        if tool.name in self.high_impact:\n756\t    45\t            return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n757\t    46\t\n758\t    47\t        return Decision(True, \"low-impact tool\", self.version)\n759\t    48\t\n760\t    49\t    async def _require_approval(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n761\t    50\t        target = tool.target_of(args)\n762\t    51\t        approval = await self.approvals.find_valid(ident, tool.name, target)\n763\t    52\t        if approval is not None:\n764\t    53\t            return Decision(True, \"approved\", self.version, approval_id=approval.id)\n765\t    54\t        approval_id = await self.approvals.request(ident, tool.name, target, args)\n766\t    55\t        return Decision(\n767\t    56\t            False,\n768\t    57\t            \"approval required; request opened\",\n769\t    58\t            self.version,\n770\t    59\t            approval_id=approval_id,\n771\t    60\t            pending=True,\n772\t    61\t        )\n773\t=== app/identity.py\n774\t     1\t\"\"\"Agent identity: who is acting, for whom, and as which agent type.\n775\t     2\t\n776\t     3\tThe agent runs under its own Kubernetes service account. Its projected\n777\t     4\tservice-account token is exchanged at the internal STS for short-lived,\n778\t     5\taudience-bound tokens. The launching user's token is never forwarded to an\n779\t     6\tintegration; the user is carried as the delegated subject of the exchange.\n780\t     7\t\"\"\"\n781\t     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n782\t     9\t\n783\t    10\timport hashlib\n784\t    11\timport json\n785\t    12\timport time\n786\t    13\timport uuid\n787\t    14\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, replace\n788\t    15\tfrom pathlib import Path\n789\t    16\t\n790\t    17\timport httpx\n791\t    18\t\n792\t    19\tfrom app.settings import Settings\n793\t    20\t\n794\t    21\tIDENTITY_FIELDS = (\n795\t    22\t    \"accountable_party\",\n796\t    23\t    \"operational_owner\",\n797\t    24\t    \"tenant\",\n798\t    25\t    \"agent_type_id\",\n799\t    26\t    \"agent_instance_id\",\n800\t    27\t    \"trace_id\",\n801\t    28\t)\n802\t    29\t\n803\t    30\t\n804\t    31\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n805\t    32\tclass RunIdentity:\n806\t    33\t    accountable_party: str\n807\t    34\t    operational_owner: str\n808\t    35\t    tenant: str\n809\t    36\t    agent_type_id: str\n810\t    37\t    agent_instance_id: str\n811\t    38\t    trace_id: str\n812\t    39\t    run_id: str\n813\t    40\t    delegated_subject: str\n814\t    41\t    agent_principal: str\n815\t    42\t    parent_instance_id: str | None = None\n816\t    43\t    role: str = \"procurement\"\n817\t    44\t\n818\t    45\t    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n819\t    46\t        for name in IDENTITY_FIELDS:\n820\t    47\t            if not getattr(self, name):\n821\t    48\t                raise ValueError(f\"identity field {name} is empty\")\n822\t    49\t\n823\t    50\t    def child(self, role: str) -> \"RunIdentity\":\n824\t    51\t        return replace(\n825\t    52\t            self,\n826\t    53\t            agent_instance_id=f\"inst-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n827\t    54\t            parent_instance_id=self.agent_instance_id,\n828\t    55\t            role=role,\n829\t    56\t        )\n830\t    57\t\n831\t    58\t\n832\t    59\tdef new_instance_id() -> str:\n833\t    60\t    return f\"inst-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n834\t    61\t\n835\t    62\t\n836\t    63\tdef compute_agent_type_id(manifest: dict) -> str:\n837\t    64\t    \"\"\"Content-derived agent type id over the frozen release manifest.\"\"\"\n838\t    65\t    material = {\n839\t    66\t        \"image_digest\": manifest[\"image\"][\"digest\"],\n840\t    67\t        \"harness_digest\": manifest[\"harness\"][\"digest\"],\n841\t    68\t        \"system_prompt\": manifest[\"prompts\"][\"system\"][\"path\"],\n842\t    69\t        \"extractor_prompt\": manifest[\"prompts\"][\"extractor\"][\"path\"],\n843\t    70\t        \"models\": manifest[\"models\"],\n844\t    71\t        \"config\": manifest[\"config\"],\n845\t    72\t        \"tools\": manifest[\"tool_pins\"],\n846\t    73\t    }\n847\t    74\t    canonical = json.dumps(material, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n848\t    75\t    return \"atid-\" + hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:40]\n849\t    76\t\n850\t    77\t\n851\t    78\t@dataclass\n852\t    79\tclass _CachedToken:\n853\t    80\t    value: str\n854\t    81\t    expires_at: float\n855\t    82\t\n856\t    83\t\n857\t    84\t@dataclass\n858\t    85\tclass TokenBroker:\n859\t    86\t    \"\"\"Exchanges the workload token for audience-bound access tokens.\"\"\"\n860\t    87\t\n861\t    88\t    settings: Settings\n862\t    89\t    _cache: dict[tuple[str, str, str], _CachedToken] = field(default_factory=dict)\n863\t    90\t\n864\t    91\t    def _workload_token(self) -> str:\n865\t    92\t        return Path(self.settings.workload_token_path).read_text().strip()\n866\t    93\t\n867\t    94\t    async def token_for(self, audience: str, scope: str, ident: RunIdentity) -> str:\n868\t    95\t        key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)\n869\t    96\t        cached = self._cache.get(key)\n870\t    97\t        if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\n871\t    98\t            return cached.value\n872\t    99\t        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0) as client:\n873\t   100\t            resp = await client.post(\n874\t   101\t                self.settings.sts_url,\n875\t   102\t                data={\n876\t   103\t                    \"grant_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange\",\n877\t   104\t                    \"subject_token\": self._workload_token(),\n878\t   105\t                    \"subject_token_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt\",\n879\t   106\t                    \"audience\": audience,\n880\t   107\t                    \"scope\": scope,\n881\t   108\t                    \"resource\": f\"urn:bu:{ident.tenant}\",\n882\t   109\t                    \"actor_token\": ident.delegated_subject,\n883\t   110\t                    \"actor_token_type\": \"urn:example:params:subject-id\",\n884\t   111\t                },\n885\t   112\t            )\n886\t   113\t            resp.raise_for_status()\n887\t   114\t            body = resp.json()\n888\t   115\t        token = _CachedToken(body[\"access_token\"], time.time() + int(body[\"expires_in\"]))\n889\t   116\t        self._cache[key] = token\n890\t   117\t        return token.value\n891\t=== app/ingest.py\n892\t     1\t\"\"\"Inbound documents: vendor quotes and invoices from the mail gateway.\n893\t     2\t\n894\t     3\tThe mail gateway posts each received message to ``/ingest/mail`` signed with\n895\t     4\tan HMAC over the timestamp and body. Accepted documents are stored per\n896\t     5\tbusiness unit and are only ever shown to the model inside an\n897\t     6\t``untrusted_document`` wrapper (tools/documents.py).\n898\t     7\t\"\"\"\n899\t     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n900\t     9\t\n901\t    10\timport base64\n902\t    11\timport email\n903\t    12\timport email.policy\n904\t    13\timport hashlib\n905\t    14\timport hmac\n906\t    15\timport io\n907\t    16\timport re\n908\t    17\timport time\n909\t    18\timport uuid\n910\t    19\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n911\t    20\tfrom pathlib import Path\n912\t    21\t\n913\t    22\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\n914\t    23\tfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n915\t    24\t\n916\t    25\trouter = APIRouter()\n917\t    26\t\n918\t    27\tMAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n919\t    28\tMAX_TEXT_CHARS = 200_000\n920\t    29\tMAX_SKEW_SECONDS = 300\n921\t    30\tALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\", \"message/rfc822\"}\n922\t    31\tSCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\"}\n923\t    32\t\n924\t    33\tINJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n925\t    34\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n926\t    35\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\n927\t    36\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\n928\t    37\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\n929\t    38\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\n930\t    39\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n931\t    40\t]\n932\t    41\t\n933\t    42\t\n934\t    43\tclass Rejected(Exception):\n935\t    44\t    pass\n936\t    45\t\n937\t    46\t\n938\t    47\t@dataclass\n939\t    48\tclass Inbound:\n940\t    49\t    business_unit: str\n941\t    50\t    sender: str\n942\t    51\t    media_type: str\n943\t    52\t    raw: bytes\n944\t    53\t\n945\t    54\t\n946\t    55\tdef verify_signature(key: bytes, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -> None:\n947\t    56\t    try:\n948\t    57\t        ts = int(timestamp)\n949\t    58\t    except ValueError as exc:\n950\t    59\t        raise Rejected(\"bad timestamp\") from exc\n951\t    60\t    if abs(time.time() - ts) > MAX_SKEW_SECONDS:\n952\t    61\t        raise Rejected(\"stale request\")\n953\t    62\t    expected = hmac.new(key, f\"{timestamp}.\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n954\t    63\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature):\n955\t    64\t        raise Rejected(\"bad signature\")\n956\t    65\t\n957\t    66\t\n958\t    67\tdef extract_text(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n959\t    68\t    if doc.media_type == \"application/pdf\":\n960\t    69\t        reader = PdfReader(io.BytesIO(doc.raw))\n961\t    70\t        if len(reader.pages) > 50:\n962\t    71\t            raise Rejected(\"too many pages\")\n963\t    72\t        return \"\\n\".join(page.extract_text() or \"\" for page in reader.pages)\n964\t    73\t    if doc.media_type == \"message/rfc822\":\n965\t    74\t        msg = email.message_from_bytes(doc.raw, policy=email.policy.default)\n966\t    75\t        body = msg.get_body(preferencelist=(\"plain\", \"html\"))\n967\t    76\t        return body.get_content() if body is not None else \"\"\n968\t    77\t    return doc.raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n969\t    78\t\n970\t    79\t\n971\t    80\tdef scan_for_injection(text: str) -> list[str]:\n972\t    81\t    return [p.pattern for p in INJECTION_PATTERNS if p.search(text)]\n973\t    82\t\n974\t    83\t\n975\t    84\tdef validate(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n976\t    85\t    if doc.media_type not in ALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n977\t    86\t        raise Rejected(f\"media type {doc.media_type} not accepted\")\n978\t    87\t    if len(doc.raw) > MAX_BODY_BYTES:\n979\t    88\t        raise Rejected(\"document too large\")\n980\t    89\t    try:\n981\t    90\t        text = extract_text(doc)\n982\t    91\t    except Rejected:\n983\t    92\t        raise\n984\t    93\t    except Exception as exc:\n985\t    94\t        raise Rejected(f\"unreadable document: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n986\t    95\t    if len(text) > MAX_TEXT_CHARS:\n987\t    96\t        raise Rejected(\"extracted text too long\")\n988\t    97\t    if doc.media_type in SCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n989\t    98\t        findings = scan_for_injection(text)\n990\t    99\t        if findings:\n991\t   100\t            raise Rejected(\"possible prompt injection: \" + \"; \".join(findings))\n992\t   101\t    return text\n993\t   102\t\n994\t   103\t\n995\t   104\t@router.post(\"/ingest/mail\")\n996\t   105\tasync def ingest_mail(request: Request) -> dict:\n997\t   106\t    body = await request.body()\n998\t   107\t    if len(body) > MAX_BODY_BYTES * 2:\n999\t   108\t        raise HTTPException(413, \"payload too large\")\n1000\t   109\t    key = Path(request.app.state.settings.mail_gateway_hmac_path).read_bytes().strip()\n1001\t   110\t    try:\n1002\t   111\t        verify_signature(\n1003\t   112\t            key,\n1004\t   113\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Timestamp\", \"\"),\n1005\t   114\t            body,\n1006\t   115\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Signature\", \"\"),\n1007\t   116\t        )\n1008\t   117\t    except Rejected as exc:\n1009\t   118\t        raise HTTPException(401, str(exc)) from exc\n1010\t   119\t\n1011\t   120\t    payload = await request.json()\n1012\t   121\t    doc = Inbound(\n1013\t   122\t        business_unit=payload[\"business_unit\"],\n1014\t   123\t        sender=payload[\"from\"],\n1015\t   124\t        media_type=payload[\"media_type\"],\n1016\t   125\t        raw=base64.b64decode(payload[\"content_b64\"], validate=True),\n1017\t   126\t    )\n1018\t   127\t    doc_id = f\"doc-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:20]}\"\n1019\t   128\t    pool = request.app.state.pool\n1020\t   129\t    try:\n1021\t   130\t        text = validate(doc)\n1022\t   131\t    except Rejected as exc:\n1023\t   132\t        await pool.execute(\n1024\t   133\t            \"\"\"\n1025\t   134\t            INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, reject_reason, received_at)\n1026\t   135\t            VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'quarantined', $6, now())\n1027\t   136\t            \"\"\",\n1028\t   137\t            doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n1029\t   138\t            hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), str(exc)[:500],\n1030\t   139\t        )\n1031\t   140\t        return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"quarantined\"}\n1032\t   141\t\n1033\t   142\t    await pool.execute(\n1034\t   143\t        \"\"\"\n1035\t   144\t        INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, text, received_at)\n1036\t   145\t        VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'accepted', $6, now())\n1037\t   146\t        \"\"\",\n1038\t   147\t        doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n1039\t   148\t        hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), text,\n1040\t   149\t    )\n1041\t   150\t    return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"accepted\"}\n1042\t=== app/killswitch.py\n1043\t     1\t\"\"\"Operator stop control.\n1044\t     2\t\n1045\t     3\tOperators halt the fleet or one business unit by setting a row in\n1046\t     4\t``control_flags`` with the ``procurement_ops`` database role (see\n1047\t     5\tops/README in the platform runbook). The agent's own database role has\n1048\t     6\tSELECT only on this table, so the agent cannot clear or delay a halt.\n1049\t     7\t\"\"\"\n1050\t     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n1051\t     9\t\n1052\t    10\t\n1053\t    11\tclass AgentHalted(Exception):\n1054\t    12\t    pass\n1055\t    13\t\n1056\t    14\t\n1057\t    15\t_QUERY = \"\"\"\n1058\t    16\tSELECT scope, reason, set_by, set_at\n1059\t    17\tFROM control_flags\n1060\t    18\tWHERE halted\n1061\t    19\t  AND (scope = 'fleet' OR scope = $1)\n1062\t    20\tORDER BY CASE WHEN scope = 'fleet' THEN 0 ELSE 1 END\n1063\t    21\tLIMIT 1\n1064\t    22\t\"\"\"\n1065\t    23\t\n1066\t    24\t\n1067\t    25\tasync def assert_running(pool, tenant: str) -> None:\n1068\t    26\t    row = await pool.fetchrow(_QUERY, f\"tenant:{tenant}\")\n1069\t    27\t    if row is not None:\n1070\t    28\t        raise AgentHalted(\n1071\t    29\t            f\"halted by {row['set_by']} at {row['set_at'].isoformat()} \"\n1072\t    30\t            f\"(scope={row['scope']}): {row['reason']}\"\n1073\t    31\t        )\n1074\t=== app/loop.py\n1075\t     1\t\"\"\"Procurement agent run loop.\n1076\t     2\t\n1077\t     3\tGraph: model turn -> (tool calls -> gate -> integration)* -> model turn ...\n1078\t     4\tEvery edge writes an audit node before the next step runs. Budgets are\n1079\t     5\tchecked before each model turn and each tool call.\n1080\t     6\t\"\"\"\n1081\t     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n1082\t     8\t\n1083\t     9\timport hashlib\n1084\t    10\timport logging\n1085\t    11\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n1086\t    12\tfrom typing import Any\n1087\t    13\t\n1088\t    14\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n1089\t    15\t\n1090\t    16\tfrom app import audit, killswitch\n1091\t    17\tfrom app.budget import Budget, BudgetExceeded\n1092\t    18\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure, measure_context\n1093\t    19\tfrom app.gate import PolicyGate\n1094\t    20\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n1095\t    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n1096\t    22\tfrom app.tools import ToolRegistry, build_registry\n1097\t    23\t\n1098\t    24\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n1099\t    25\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.loop\")\n1100\t    26\t\n1101\t    27\tCOMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES = 40\n1102\t    28\tKEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES = 12\n1103\t    29\t\n1104\t    30\t\n1105\t    31\t@dataclass\n1106\t    32\tclass AgentDeps:\n1107\t    33\t    settings: Any\n1108\t    34\t    pool: Any\n1109\t    35\t    gate: PolicyGate\n1110\t    36\t    erp: Any\n1111\t    37\t    slack: Any\n1112\t    38\t    broker: Any\n1113\t    39\t    extractor: Any = None\n1114\t    40\t    _budgets: dict[str, Budget] = field(default_factory=dict)\n1115\t    41\t    _contexts: dict[str, ContextMeasure] = field(default_factory=dict)\n1116\t    42\t\n1117\t    43\t    def current_budget(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> Budget:\n1118\t    44\t        return self._budgets[ident.run_id]\n1119\t    45\t\n1120\t    46\t    def current_context(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> ContextMeasure:\n1121\t    47\t        return self._contexts.get(ident.agent_instance_id, ContextMeasure.unavailable())\n1122\t    48\t\n1123\t    49\t    def erp_scope_for(self, operation: str) -> str:\n1124\t    50\t        scopes = self.settings.policy[\"erp\"][\"operation_scopes\"]\n1125\t    51\t        return scopes.get(operation, \"erp.read\")\n1126\t    52\t\n1127\t    53\t    async def execute_tool(self, ident, registry: ToolRegistry, use, parent: str, ctx: ContextMeasure) -> dict:\n1128\t    54\t        self._contexts[ident.agent_instance_id] = ctx\n1129\t    55\t        proposed = await audit.record(\n1130\t    56\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_proposed\", parent=parent, context=ctx,\n1131\t    57\t            payload={\"tool\": use.name, \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"args\": audit.summarize_args(use.input)},\n1132\t    58\t        )\n1133\t    59\t        tool = registry.get(use.name)\n1134\t    60\t        if tool is None:\n1135\t    61\t            await audit.record(\n1136\t    62\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_denied\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n1137\t    63\t                policy_version=self.gate.version, payload={\"reason\": \"tool not in role allowlist\"},\n1138\t    64\t            )\n1139\t    65\t            return _error(use.id, f\"tool {use.name} is not available to this agent\")\n1140\t    66\t\n1141\t    67\t        decision = await self.gate.authorize(ident, tool, use.input)\n1142\t    68\t        authz = await audit.record(\n1143\t    69\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"authz_decision\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n1144\t    70\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n1145\t    71\t            payload={\"allow\": decision.allow, \"reason\": decision.reason, \"pending\": decision.pending},\n1146\t    72\t        )\n1147\t    73\t        if not decision.allow:\n1148\t    74\t            if decision.pending:\n1149\t    75\t                return _error(use.id, f\"approval requested ({decision.approval_id}); do not retry until approved\")\n1150\t    76\t            return _error(use.id, f\"denied: {decision.reason}\")\n1151\t    77\t\n1152\t    78\t        operation_id = f\"op-{hashlib.sha256((authz + use.id).encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}\"\n1153\t    79\t        try:\n1154\t    80\t            with tracer.start_as_current_span(f\"execute_tool {use.name}\") as span:\n1155\t    81\t                for k, v in ctx.otel_attributes().items():\n1156\t    82\t                    span.set_attribute(k, v)\n1157\t    83\t                output = await tool.invoke(use.input, ident)\n1158\t    84\t        except BudgetExceeded:\n1159\t    85\t            raise\n1160\t    86\t        except Exception as exc:\n1161\t    87\t            await audit.record(\n1162\t    88\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_error\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n1163\t    89\t                policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n1164\t    90\t                operation_id=operation_id,\n1165\t    91\t                payload={\"error_type\": type(exc).__name__, \"error\": str(exc)[:500]},\n1166\t    92\t            )\n1167\t    93\t            return _error(use.id, f\"{use.name} failed: {type(exc).__name__}\")\n1168\t    94\t\n1169\t    95\t        await audit.record(\n1170\t    96\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_result\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n1171\t    97\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n1172\t    98\t            operation_id=operation_id,\n1173\t    99\t            payload={\"result_sha256\": audit.digest(output), \"result\": output},\n1174\t   100\t        )\n1175\t   101\t        return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"content\": redact_for_model(output)}\n1176\t   102\t\n1177\t   103\t\n1178\t   104\tdef _error(tool_use_id: str, message: str) -> dict:\n1179\t   105\t    return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": tool_use_id, \"is_error\": True, \"content\": message}\n1180\t   106\t\n1181\t   107\t\n1182\t   108\tdef _compact(messages: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], bool]:\n1183\t   109\t    if len(messages) <= COMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES:\n1184\t   110\t        return messages, False\n1185\t   111\t    head, tail = messages[:1], messages[-KEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES:]\n1186\t   112\t    while tail and tail[0][\"role\"] != \"assistant\":\n1187\t   113\t        tail = tail[1:]\n1188\t   114\t    note = {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[earlier tool exchanges were removed to save space]\"}\n1189\t   115\t    return head + [note] + tail, True\n1190\t   116\t\n1191\t   117\t\n1192\t   118\tclass ProcurementAgent:\n1193\t   119\t    def __init__(self, *, client, deps: AgentDeps, system_prompt: str, role: str = \"procurement\"):\n1194\t   120\t        self.client = client\n1195\t   121\t        self.deps = deps\n1196\t   122\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n1197\t   123\t        self.role = role\n1198\t   124\t\n1199\t   125\t    async def run(self, ident: RunIdentity, task: str) -> str | None:\n1200\t   126\t        pool = self.deps.pool\n1201\t   127\t        await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n1202\t   128\t        budget = Budget.for_run(self.deps.settings.budgets, ident)\n1203\t   129\t        await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n1204\t   130\t        self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n1205\t   131\t        registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n1206\t   132\t\n1207\t   133\t        run_node = await audit.record(\n1208\t   134\t            pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n1209\t   135\t            payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n1210\t   136\t        )\n1211\t   137\t        messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n1212\t   138\t        try:\n1213\t   139\t            while True:\n1214\t   140\t                budget.check_step()\n1215\t   141\t                messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\n1216\t   142\t                request = {\n1217\t   143\t                    \"model\": self.deps.settings.model_id,\n1218\t   144\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n1219\t   145\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n1220\t   146\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n1221\t   147\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n1222\t   148\t                }\n1223\t   149\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted)\n1224\t   150\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n1225\t   151\t                budget.charge_model(self.deps.settings.model_id, response.usage)\n1226\t   152\t                await budget.flush(pool)\n1227\t   153\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n1228\t   154\t                decision = await audit.record(\n1229\t   155\t                    pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n1230\t   156\t                    payload={\n1231\t   157\t                        \"requested_model\": request[\"model\"],\n1232\t   158\t                        \"served_model\": response.model,\n1233\t   159\t                        \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason,\n1234\t   160\t                        \"proposed_tools\": [b.name for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"],\n1235\t   161\t                    },\n1236\t   162\t                )\n1237\t   163\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n1238\t   164\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n1239\t   165\t                if not uses:\n1240\t   166\t                    final = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n1241\t   167\t                    await audit.record(pool, ident, kind=\"run_finished\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n1242\t   168\t                                       payload={\"final_sha256\": audit.digest(final)})\n1243\t   169\t                    return final\n1244\t   170\t                results = []\n1245\t   171\t                for use in uses:\n1246\t   172\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n1247\t   173\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n1248\t   174\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n1249\t   175\t        except BudgetExceeded as exc:\n1250\t   176\t            await audit.record(\n1251\t   177\t                pool, ident, kind=\"budget_exceeded\", parent=run_node,\n1252\t   178\t                payload={\"limit\": exc.limit, \"used\": str(exc.used), \"allowed\": str(exc.allowed)},\n1253\t   179\t            )\n1254\t   180\t            await self.deps.slack.post(\n1255\t   181\t                channel=\"#procurement-agent-ops\",\n1256\t   182\t                text=f\"Run {ident.run_id} ({ident.tenant}) stopped: {exc.limit} exceeded.\",\n1257\t   183\t            )\n1258\t   184\t            return None\n1259\t   185\t        finally:\n1260\t   186\t            self.deps._budgets.pop(ident.run_id, None)\n1261\t=== app/main.py\n1262\t     1\t\"\"\"FastAPI entry point for the procurement agent.\"\"\"\n1263\t     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n1264\t     3\t\n1265\t     4\timport asyncio\n1266\t     5\timport hashlib\n1267\t     6\timport hmac\n1268\t     7\timport json\n1269\t     8\timport logging\n1270\t     9\timport time\n1271\t    10\timport uuid\n1272\t    11\tfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n1273\t    12\tfrom pathlib import Path\n1274\t    13\tfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs\n1275\t    14\t\n1276\t    15\timport asyncpg\n1277\t    16\timport jwt\n1278\t    17\tfrom anthropic import AsyncAnthropic\n1279\t    18\tfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, HTTPException, Request\n1280\t    19\tfrom fastapi.security import HTTPAuthorizationCredentials, HTTPBearer\n1281\t    20\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n1282\t    21\tfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n1283\t    22\t\n1284\t    23\tfrom app import audit, ingest\n1285\t    24\tfrom app.approvals import ApprovalStore, ApproverNotAuthorized\n1286\t    25\tfrom app.extractor import LineItemExtractor\n1287\t    26\tfrom app.gate import PolicyGate\n1288\t    27\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity, TokenBroker, new_instance_id\n1289\t    28\tfrom app.loop import AgentDeps, ProcurementAgent\n1290\t    29\tfrom app.mcp_client import ErpMcpClient\n1291\t    30\tfrom app.redact import RedactingFilter\n1292\t    31\tfrom app.settings import get_settings\n1293\t    32\tfrom app.startup import startup_checks\n1294\t    33\tfrom app.tools.slack import SlackClient\n1295\t    34\t\n1296\t    35\tlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\"%(asctime)s %(levelname)s %(name)s %(message)s\")\n1297\t    36\tfor handler in logging.getLogger().handlers:\n1298\t    37\t    handler.addFilter(RedactingFilter())\n1299\t    38\tlog = logging.getLogger(\"procurement\")\n1300\t    39\t\n1301\t    40\tAGENT_PRINCIPAL = \"spiffe://example-corp.test/ns/procurement-prod/sa/procurement-agent\"\n1302\t    41\tbearer = HTTPBearer()\n1303\t    42\t\n1304\t    43\t\n1305\t    44\tclass RunRequest(BaseModel):\n1306\t    45\t    task: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=4000)\n1307\t    46\t    department: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=64)\n1308\t    47\t\n1309\t    48\t\n1310\t    49\tclass Principal(BaseModel):\n1311\t    50\t    subject: str\n1312\t    51\t    business_unit: str\n1313\t    52\t\n1314\t    53\t\n1315\t    54\tdef service_identity(settings, agent_type_id: str, tenant: str = \"system\") -> RunIdentity:\n1316\t    55\t    return RunIdentity(\n1317\t    56\t        accountable_party=\"system:procurement-agent\",\n1318\t    57\t        operational_owner=settings.operational_owner,\n1319\t    58\t        tenant=tenant,\n1320\t    59\t        agent_type_id=agent_type_id,\n1321\t    60\t        agent_instance_id=new_instance_id(),\n1322\t    61\t        trace_id=uuid.uuid4().hex,\n1323\t    62\t        run_id=f\"bg-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n1324\t    63\t        delegated_subject=\"system:procurement-agent\",\n1325\t    64\t        agent_principal=AGENT_PRINCIPAL,\n1326\t    65\t    )\n1327\t    66\t\n1328\t    67\t\n1329\t    68\tasync def expire_approvals_forever(app: FastAPI) -> None:\n1330\t    69\t    while True:\n1331\t    70\t        await asyncio.sleep(60)\n1332\t    71\t        ident = service_identity(app.state.settings, app.state.agent_type_id)\n1333\t    72\t        count = await app.state.pool.fetchval(\n1334\t    73\t            \"WITH e AS (UPDATE approvals SET status = 'expired' \"\n1335\t    74\t            \"WHERE status = 'pending' AND expires_at <= now() RETURNING 1) SELECT count(*) FROM e\"\n1336\t    75\t        )\n1337\t    76\t        await audit.record(app.state.pool, ident, kind=\"background_job\",\n1338\t    77\t                           payload={\"job\": \"expire_approvals\", \"expired\": count})\n1339\t    78\t\n1340\t    79\t\n1341\t    80\t@asynccontextmanager\n1342\t    81\tasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n1343\t    82\t    settings = get_settings()\n1344\t    83\t    agent_type_id = startup_checks(settings)\n1345\t    84\t    pool = await asyncpg.create_pool(settings.database_url, min_size=2, max_size=10)\n1346\t    85\t    broker = TokenBroker(settings)\n1347\t    86\t\n1348\t    87\t    async def slack_token() -> str:\n1349\t    88\t        return await broker.token_for(\"slack-proxy\", \"chat:write\", service_identity(settings, agent_type_id))\n1350\t    89\t\n1351\t    90\t    slack = SlackClient(settings.slack_api_url, slack_token)\n1352\t    91\t    approvals = ApprovalStore(pool, settings.policy, slack)\n1353\t    92\t    gate = PolicyGate(settings.policy, approvals)\n1354\t    93\t    erp = ErpMcpClient(settings.erp_mcp_url, settings.manifest[\"tool_pins\"], broker)\n1355\t    94\t    await erp.initialize(service_identity(settings, agent_type_id))\n1356\t    95\t\n1357\t    96\t    client = AsyncAnthropic()\n1358\t    97\t    deps = AgentDeps(settings=settings, pool=pool, gate=gate, erp=erp, slack=slack, broker=broker)\n1359\t    98\t    deps.extractor = LineItemExtractor(\n1360\t    99\t        client=client, settings=settings, deps=deps,\n1361\t   100\t        system_prompt=(settings.prompt_dir / \"extractor.md\").read_text(),\n1362\t   101\t    )\n1363\t   102\t    app.state.settings = settings\n1364\t   103\t    app.state.pool = pool\n1365\t   104\t    app.state.agent_type_id = agent_type_id\n1366\t   105\t    app.state.approvals = approvals\n1367\t   106\t    app.state.agent = ProcurementAgent(\n1368\t   107\t        client=client, deps=deps, system_prompt=(settings.prompt_dir / \"system.md\").read_text()\n1369\t   108\t    )\n1370\t   109\t    app.state.jwks = jwt.PyJWKClient(settings.oidc_jwks_url, cache_keys=True, lifespan=300)\n1371\t   110\t    sweeper = asyncio.create_task(expire_approvals_forever(app))\n1372\t   111\t    try:\n1373\t   112\t        yield\n1374\t   113\t    finally:\n1375\t   114\t        sweeper.cancel()\n1376\t   115\t        await pool.close()\n1377\t   116\t\n1378\t   117\t\n1379\t   118\tapp = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)\n1380\t   119\tapp.include_router(ingest.router)\n1381\t   120\t\n1382\t   121\t\n1383\t   122\tdef authenticate(request: Request, creds: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials = Depends(bearer)) -> Principal:\n1384\t   123\t    settings = request.app.state.settings\n1385\t   124\t    try:\n1386\t   125\t        key = request.app.state.jwks.get_signing_key_from_jwt(creds.credentials)\n1387\t   126\t        claims = jwt.decode(\n1388\t   127\t            creds.credentials,\n1389\t   128\t            key.key,\n1390\t   129\t            algorithms=[\"RS256\", \"ES256\"],\n1391\t   130\t            audience=settings.oidc_audience,\n1392\t   131\t            issuer=settings.oidc_issuer,\n1393\t   132\t            options={\"require\": [\"exp\", \"iat\", \"sub\", \"aud\", \"iss\"]},\n1394\t   133\t        )\n1395\t   134\t    except jwt.PyJWTError as exc:\n1396\t   135\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"invalid token\") from exc\n1397\t   136\t    bu = claims.get(\"bu\")\n1398\t   137\t    if not bu:\n1399\t   138\t        raise HTTPException(403, \"token has no business unit\")\n1400\t   139\t    return Principal(subject=claims[\"sub\"], business_unit=bu)\n1401\t   140\t\n1402\t   141\t\n1403\t   142\t@app.post(\"/runs\")\n1404\t   143\tasync def start_run(req: RunRequest, request: Request, principal: Principal = Depends(authenticate)) -> dict:\n1405\t   144\t    settings = request.app.state.settings\n1406\t   145\t    span_ctx = trace.get_current_span().get_span_context()\n1407\t   146\t    trace_id = format(span_ctx.trace_id, \"032x\") if span_ctx.is_valid else uuid.uuid4().hex\n1408\t   147\t    ident = RunIdentity(\n1409\t   148\t        accountable_party=principal.subject,\n1410\t   149\t        operational_owner=settings.operational_owner,\n1411\t   150\t        tenant=principal.business_unit,\n1412\t   151\t        agent_type_id=request.app.state.agent_type_id,\n1413\t   152\t        agent_instance_id=new_instance_id(),\n1414\t   153\t        trace_id=trace_id,\n1415\t   154\t        run_id=f\"run-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n1416\t   155\t        delegated_subject=principal.subject,\n1417\t   156\t        agent_principal=AGENT_PRINCIPAL,\n1418\t   157\t    )\n1419\t   158\t    task = f\"Department: {req.department}\\n\\n{req.task}\"\n1420\t   159\t    asyncio.create_task(request.app.state.agent.run(ident, task))\n1421\t   160\t    return {\"run_id\": ident.run_id, \"agent_instance_id\": ident.agent_instance_id}\n1422\t   161\t\n1423\t   162\t\n1424\t   163\t@app.post(\"/slack/interactions\")\n1425\t   164\tasync def slack_interactions(request: Request) -> dict:\n1426\t   165\t    body = await request.body()\n1427\t   166\t    timestamp = request.headers.get(\"X-Slack-Request-Timestamp\", \"0\")\n1428\t   167\t    if abs(time.time() - int(timestamp)) > 300:\n1429\t   168\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"stale request\")\n1430\t   169\t    secret = Path(request.app.state.settings.slack_signing_secret_path).read_bytes().strip()\n1431\t   170\t    expected = \"v0=\" + hmac.new(secret, f\"v0:{timestamp}:\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n1432\t   171\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, request.headers.get(\"X-Slack-Signature\", \"\")):\n1433\t   172\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"bad signature\")\n1434\t   173\t\n1435\t   174\t    payload = json.loads(parse_qs(body.decode())[\"payload\"][0])\n1436\t   175\t    action = payload[\"actions\"][0]\n1437\t   176\t    slack_user = payload[\"user\"][\"id\"]\n1438\t   177\t    row = await request.app.state.pool.fetchrow(\n1439\t   178\t        \"SELECT email, role FROM approvers WHERE slack_user_id = $1 AND active\", slack_user\n1440\t   179\t    )\n1441\t   180\t    if row is None:\n1442\t   181\t        raise HTTPException(403, \"not an approver\")\n1443\t   182\t    try:\n1444\t   183\t        await request.app.state.approvals.decide(\n1445\t   184\t            action[\"value\"], approver=row[\"email\"], approver_role=row[\"role\"],\n1446\t   185\t            approve=action[\"action_id\"] == \"approve\",\n1447\t   186\t        )\n1448\t   187\t    except ApproverNotAuthorized as exc:\n1449\t   188\t        raise HTTPException(403, str(exc)) from exc\n1450\t   189\t    except ValueError as exc:\n1451\t   190\t        raise HTTPException(409, str(exc)) from exc\n1452\t   191\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n1453\t   192\t\n1454\t   193\t\n1455\t   194\t@app.get(\"/healthz\")\n1456\t   195\tasync def healthz() -> dict:\n1457\t   196\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n1458\t=== app/mcp_client.py\n1459\t     1\t\"\"\"Client for the ERP MCP server, reached through the internal MCP gateway.\n1460\t     2\t\n1461\t     3\tOn startup the tool list is fetched and each tool's description and input\n1462\t     4\tschema are fingerprinted and compared with the pins in the release manifest.\n1463\t     5\tAny unpinned or changed tool stops startup. Tool metadata is also scanned for\n1464\t     6\tinstruction-like content before any of it is shown to the model.\n1465\t     7\t\"\"\"\n1466\t     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n1467\t     9\t\n1468\t    10\timport hashlib\n1469\t    11\timport json\n1470\t    12\timport logging\n1471\t    13\timport re\n1472\t    14\timport uuid\n1473\t    15\tfrom typing import Any\n1474\t    16\t\n1475\t    17\timport httpx\n1476\t    18\t\n1477\t    19\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity, TokenBroker\n1478\t    20\tfrom app.redact import redact_text\n1479\t    21\t\n1480\t    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n1481\t    23\t\n1482\t    24\tMAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS = 1024\n1483\t    25\tSUSPICIOUS_METADATA = [\n1484\t    26\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|previous|prior) instructions\"),\n1485\t    27\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are now|act as)\\b\"),\n1486\t    28\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(before|instead of) (calling|using) \\w+\\.\\w+\"),\n1487\t    29\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n1488\t    30\t    re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\"),\n1489\t    31\t]\n1490\t    32\t\n1491\t    33\t\n1492\t    34\tclass ToolPinMismatch(Exception):\n1493\t    35\t    pass\n1494\t    36\t\n1495\t    37\t\n1496\t    38\tclass UnknownErpOperation(Exception):\n1497\t    39\t    pass\n1498\t    40\t\n1499\t    41\t\n1500\t    42\tdef fingerprint(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n1501\t    43\t    material = {\n1502\t    44\t        \"name\": tool[\"name\"],\n1503\t    45\t        \"description\": tool.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n1504\t    46\t        \"inputSchema\": tool.get(\"inputSchema\", {}),\n1505\t    47\t        \"annotations\": tool.get(\"annotations\", {}),\n1506\t    48\t    }\n1507\t    49\t    raw = json.dumps(material, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n1508\t    50\t    return \"sha256:\" + hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n1509\t    51\t\n1510\t    52\t\n1511\t    53\tdef scan_metadata(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n1512\t    54\t    description = tool.get(\"description\", \"\")\n1513\t    55\t    if len(description) > MAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS:\n1514\t    56\t        raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: description too long\")\n1515\t    57\t    blob = json.dumps(tool, ensure_ascii=False)\n1516\t    58\t    for pattern in SUSPICIOUS_METADATA:\n1517\t    59\t        if pattern.search(blob):\n1518\t    60\t            raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: suspicious metadata ({pattern.pattern})\")\n1519\t    61\t\n1520\t    62\t\n1521\t    63\tclass ErpMcpClient:\n1522\t    64\t    AUDIENCE = \"erp-mcp-gateway\"\n1523\t    65\t\n1524\t    66\t    def __init__(self, url: str, pins: dict[str, str], broker: TokenBroker):\n1525\t    67\t        self.url = url\n1526\t    68\t        self.pins = pins\n1527\t    69\t        self.broker = broker\n1528\t    70\t        self._tools: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n1529\t    71\t\n1530\t    72\t    async def _rpc(self, method: str, params: dict[str, Any], token: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n1531\t    73\t        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=20.0, follow_redirects=False) as client:\n1532\t    74\t            resp = await client.post(\n1533\t    75\t                self.url,\n1534\t    76\t                json={\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": str(uuid.uuid4()), \"method\": method, \"params\": params},\n1535\t    77\t                headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Mcp-Protocol-Version\": \"2025-06-18\"},\n1536\t    78\t            )\n1537\t    79\t        resp.raise_for_status()\n1538\t    80\t        if len(resp.content) > 512_000:\n1539\t    81\t            raise ValueError(\"erp response too large\")\n1540\t    82\t        body = resp.json()\n1541\t    83\t        if \"error\" in body:\n1542\t    84\t            raise RuntimeError(f\"erp error {body['error'].get('code')}: {redact_text(str(body['error'].get('message')))}\")\n1543\t    85\t        return body[\"result\"]\n1544\t    86\t\n1545\t    87\t    async def _list_tools(self, token: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n1546\t    88\t        result = await self._rpc(\"tools/list\", {}, token)\n1547\t    89\t        return list(result.get(\"tools\", []))\n1548\t    90\t\n1549\t    91\t    async def initialize(self, service_ident: RunIdentity) -> None:\n1550\t    92\t        token = await self.broker.token_for(self.AUDIENCE, \"erp.tools.list\", service_ident)\n1551\t    93\t        tools = await self._list_tools(token)\n1552\t    94\t        for tool in tools:\n1553\t    95\t            expected = self.pins.get(tool[\"name\"])\n1554\t    96\t            actual = fingerprint(tool)\n1555\t    97\t            if expected != actual:\n1556\t    98\t                raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: expected {expected}, got {actual}\")\n1557\t    99\t            scan_metadata(tool)\n1558\t   100\t        self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}\n1559\t   101\t        log.info(\"erp tools loaded: %d\", len(self._tools))\n1560\t   102\t\n1561\t   103\t    async def on_notification(self, message: dict[str, Any], service_ident: RunIdentity) -> None:\n1562\t   104\t        if message.get(\"method\") == \"notifications/tools/list_changed\":\n1563\t   105\t            await self.refresh_tools(service_ident)\n1564\t   106\t\n1565\t   107\t    async def refresh_tools(self, service_ident: RunIdentity) -> None:\n1566\t   108\t        token = await self.broker.token_for(self.AUDIENCE, \"erp.tools.list\", service_ident)\n1567\t   109\t        tools = await self._list_tools(token)\n1568\t   110\t        self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}\n1569\t   111\t        log.info(\"erp tools refreshed: %d\", len(self._tools))\n1570\t   112\t\n1571\t   113\t    def operations(self) -> list[str]:\n1572\t   114\t        return sorted(self._tools)\n1573\t   115\t\n1574\t   116\t    async def call(self, operation: str, arguments: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity, scope: str) -> Any:\n1575\t   117\t        if operation not in self._tools:\n1576\t   118\t            raise UnknownErpOperation(operation)\n1577\t   119\t        token = await self.broker.token_for(self.AUDIENCE, scope, ident)\n1578\t   120\t        result = await self._rpc(\n1579\t   121\t            \"tools/call\",\n1580\t   122\t            {\n1581\t   123\t                \"name\": operation,\n1582\t   124\t                \"arguments\": arguments,\n1583\t   125\t                \"_meta\": {\"business_unit\": ident.tenant, \"run_id\": ident.run_id},\n1584\t   126\t            },\n1585\t   127\t            token,\n1586\t   128\t        )\n1587\t   129\t        if result.get(\"isError\"):\n1588\t   130\t            raise RuntimeError(redact_text(json.dumps(result.get(\"content\", []))))\n1589\t   131\t        return result.get(\"structuredContent\") or result.get(\"content\")\n1590\t=== app/redact.py\n1591\t     1\t\"\"\"Redaction for model input, logs, audit payloads, and outbound messages.\n1592\t     2\t\n1593\t     3\tApplied in four places:\n1594\t     4\t  * tool results before they are appended to the model context (loop.py)\n1595\t     5\t  * every audit payload (audit.py)\n1596\t     6\t  * the root logging filter (main.py)\n1597\t     7\t  * outbound Slack text (tools/slack.py)\n1598\t     8\t\"\"\"\n1599\t     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff","uuid":"6d4dcdcf-d895-42c6-b5f4-ca71742f6ef0","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:24:06.151Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-repeat-z0r2wndt/7b08f688-90d5-4b4c-af7c-eac511a967ff/tool-results/bsj8ssif6.txt","content":"   104\t        data = json.loads(text)\n   105\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n   106\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor returned non-JSON output\") from exc\n   107\t    if not isinstance(data, list) or len(data) > 500:\n   108\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor output must be a list of at most 500 items\")\n   109\t    items = []\n   110\t    for raw in data:\n   111\t        if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not set(raw) <= LINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS:\n   112\t            raise ExtractionFailed(\"unexpected line-item fields\")\n   113\t        items.append({k: redact_for_model(v) if isinstance(v, str) else v for k, v in raw.items()})\n   114\t    return items\n=== app/gate.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Policy gate for tool calls.\n     2\t\n     3\tRuns in the harness between the model's proposed call and the integration.\n     4\tHigh-impact operations are denied unless a valid approval exists; when none\n     5\texists an approval request is opened and the call returns as pending.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    10\tfrom typing import Any\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom app.approvals import ApprovalStore\n    13\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    17\tclass Decision:\n    18\t    allow: bool\n    19\t    reason: str\n    20\t    policy_version: str\n    21\t    approval_id: str | None = None\n    22\t    pending: bool = False\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tclass PolicyGate:\n    26\t    def __init__(self, policy: dict, approvals: ApprovalStore):\n    27\t        self.version: str = policy[\"version\"]\n    28\t        self.high_impact: frozenset[str] = frozenset(policy[\"high_impact_tools\"])\n    29\t        self.erp_read_prefixes: tuple[str, ...] = tuple(policy[\"erp\"][\"read_prefixes\"])\n    30\t        self.approvals = approvals\n    31\t\n    32\t    async def authorize(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n    33\t        if tool.name == \"erp_call\":\n    34\t            operation = str(args.get(\"operation\", \"\"))\n    35\t            if not operation.startswith(self.erp_read_prefixes):\n    36\t                return Decision(False, f\"erp operation not permitted: {operation}\", self.version)\n    37\t            return Decision(True, \"erp read operation\", self.version)\n    38\t\n    39\t        if tool.name == \"post_slack_message\":\n    40\t            if args.get(\"external\", False):\n    41\t                return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n    42\t            return Decision(True, \"internal staff message\", self.version)\n    43\t\n    44\t        if tool.name in self.high_impact:\n    45\t            return await self._require_approval(ident, tool, args)\n    46\t\n    47\t        return Decision(True, \"low-impact tool\", self.version)\n    48\t\n    49\t    async def _require_approval(self, ident: RunIdentity, tool, args: dict[str, Any]) -> Decision:\n    50\t        target = tool.target_of(args)\n    51\t        approval = await self.approvals.find_valid(ident, tool.name, target)\n    52\t        if approval is not None:\n    53\t            return Decision(True, \"approved\", self.version, approval_id=approval.id)\n    54\t        approval_id = await self.approvals.request(ident, tool.name, target, args)\n    55\t        return Decision(\n    56\t            False,\n    57\t            \"approval required; request opened\",\n    58\t            self.version,\n    59\t            approval_id=approval_id,\n    60\t            pending=True,\n    61\t        )\n=== app/identity.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Agent identity: who is acting, for whom, and as which agent type.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe agent runs under its own Kubernetes service account. Its projected\n     4\tservice-account token is exchanged at the internal STS for short-lived,\n     5\taudience-bound tokens. The launching user's token is never forwarded to an\n     6\tintegration; the user is carried as the delegated subject of the exchange.\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport hashlib\n    11\timport json\n    12\timport time\n    13\timport uuid\n    14\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, replace\n    15\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    16\t\n    17\timport httpx\n    18\t\n    19\tfrom app.settings import Settings\n    20\t\n    21\tIDENTITY_FIELDS = (\n    22\t    \"accountable_party\",\n    23\t    \"operational_owner\",\n    24\t    \"tenant\",\n    25\t    \"agent_type_id\",\n    26\t    \"agent_instance_id\",\n    27\t    \"trace_id\",\n    28\t)\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    32\tclass RunIdentity:\n    33\t    accountable_party: str\n    34\t    operational_owner: str\n    35\t    tenant: str\n    36\t    agent_type_id: str\n    37\t    agent_instance_id: str\n    38\t    trace_id: str\n    39\t    run_id: str\n    40\t    delegated_subject: str\n    41\t    agent_principal: str\n    42\t    parent_instance_id: str | None = None\n    43\t    role: str = \"procurement\"\n    44\t\n    45\t    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\n    46\t        for name in IDENTITY_FIELDS:\n    47\t            if not getattr(self, name):\n    48\t                raise ValueError(f\"identity field {name} is empty\")\n    49\t\n    50\t    def child(self, role: str) -> \"RunIdentity\":\n    51\t        return replace(\n    52\t            self,\n    53\t            agent_instance_id=f\"inst-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n    54\t            parent_instance_id=self.agent_instance_id,\n    55\t            role=role,\n    56\t        )\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef new_instance_id() -> str:\n    60\t    return f\"inst-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef compute_agent_type_id(manifest: dict) -> str:\n    64\t    \"\"\"Content-derived agent type id over the frozen release manifest.\"\"\"\n    65\t    material = {\n    66\t        \"image_digest\": manifest[\"image\"][\"digest\"],\n    67\t        \"harness_digest\": manifest[\"harness\"][\"digest\"],\n    68\t        \"system_prompt\": manifest[\"prompts\"][\"system\"][\"path\"],\n    69\t        \"extractor_prompt\": manifest[\"prompts\"][\"extractor\"][\"path\"],\n    70\t        \"models\": manifest[\"models\"],\n    71\t        \"config\": manifest[\"config\"],\n    72\t        \"tools\": manifest[\"tool_pins\"],\n    73\t    }\n    74\t    canonical = json.dumps(material, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n    75\t    return \"atid-\" + hashlib.sha256(canonical.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:40]\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t@dataclass\n    79\tclass _CachedToken:\n    80\t    value: str\n    81\t    expires_at: float\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\t@dataclass\n    85\tclass TokenBroker:\n    86\t    \"\"\"Exchanges the workload token for audience-bound access tokens.\"\"\"\n    87\t\n    88\t    settings: Settings\n    89\t    _cache: dict[tuple[str, str, str], _CachedToken] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    90\t\n    91\t    def _workload_token(self) -> str:\n    92\t        return Path(self.settings.workload_token_path).read_text().strip()\n    93\t\n    94\t    async def token_for(self, audience: str, scope: str, ident: RunIdentity) -> str:\n    95\t        key = (audience, scope, ident.tenant)\n    96\t        cached = self._cache.get(key)\n    97\t        if cached and cached.expires_at - 30 > time.time():\n    98\t            return cached.value\n    99\t        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0) as client:\n   100\t            resp = await client.post(\n   101\t                self.settings.sts_url,\n   102\t                data={\n   103\t                    \"grant_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:token-exchange\",\n   104\t                    \"subject_token\": self._workload_token(),\n   105\t                    \"subject_token_type\": \"urn:ietf:params:oauth:token-type:jwt\",\n   106\t                    \"audience\": audience,\n   107\t                    \"scope\": scope,\n   108\t                    \"resource\": f\"urn:bu:{ident.tenant}\",\n   109\t                    \"actor_token\": ident.delegated_subject,\n   110\t                    \"actor_token_type\": \"urn:example:params:subject-id\",\n   111\t                },\n   112\t            )\n   113\t            resp.raise_for_status()\n   114\t            body = resp.json()\n   115\t        token = _CachedToken(body[\"access_token\"], time.time() + int(body[\"expires_in\"]))\n   116\t        self._cache[key] = token\n   117\t        return token.value\n=== app/ingest.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Inbound documents: vendor quotes and invoices from the mail gateway.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe mail gateway posts each received message to ``/ingest/mail`` signed with\n     4\tan HMAC over the timestamp and body. Accepted documents are stored per\n     5\tbusiness unit and are only ever shown to the model inside an\n     6\t``untrusted_document`` wrapper (tools/documents.py).\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport base64\n    11\timport email\n    12\timport email.policy\n    13\timport hashlib\n    14\timport hmac\n    15\timport io\n    16\timport re\n    17\timport time\n    18\timport uuid\n    19\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    20\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    21\t\n    22\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\n    23\tfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n    24\t\n    25\trouter = APIRouter()\n    26\t\n    27\tMAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n    28\tMAX_TEXT_CHARS = 200_000\n    29\tMAX_SKEW_SECONDS = 300\n    30\tALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\", \"message/rfc822\"}\n    31\tSCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\"}\n    32\t\n    33\tINJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n    34\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n    35\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\n    36\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\n    37\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\n    38\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\n    39\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n    40\t]\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tclass Rejected(Exception):\n    44\t    pass\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t@dataclass\n    48\tclass Inbound:\n    49\t    business_unit: str\n    50\t    sender: str\n    51\t    media_type: str\n    52\t    raw: bytes\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef verify_signature(key: bytes, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -> None:\n    56\t    try:\n    57\t        ts = int(timestamp)\n    58\t    except ValueError as exc:\n    59\t        raise Rejected(\"bad timestamp\") from exc\n    60\t    if abs(time.time() - ts) > MAX_SKEW_SECONDS:\n    61\t        raise Rejected(\"stale request\")\n    62\t    expected = hmac.new(key, f\"{timestamp}.\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    63\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature):\n    64\t        raise Rejected(\"bad signature\")\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef extract_text(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    68\t    if doc.media_type == \"application/pdf\":\n    69\t        reader = PdfReader(io.BytesIO(doc.raw))\n    70\t        if len(reader.pages) > 50:\n    71\t            raise Rejected(\"too many pages\")\n    72\t        return \"\\n\".join(page.extract_text() or \"\" for page in reader.pages)\n    73\t    if doc.media_type == \"message/rfc822\":\n    74\t        msg = email.message_from_bytes(doc.raw, policy=email.policy.default)\n    75\t        body = msg.get_body(preferencelist=(\"plain\", \"html\"))\n    76\t        return body.get_content() if body is not None else \"\"\n    77\t    return doc.raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef scan_for_injection(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    81\t    return [p.pattern for p in INJECTION_PATTERNS if p.search(text)]\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\tdef validate(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    85\t    if doc.media_type not in ALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    86\t        raise Rejected(f\"media type {doc.media_type} not accepted\")\n    87\t    if len(doc.raw) > MAX_BODY_BYTES:\n    88\t        raise Rejected(\"document too large\")\n    89\t    try:\n    90\t        text = extract_text(doc)\n    91\t    except Rejected:\n    92\t        raise\n    93\t    except Exception as exc:\n    94\t        raise Rejected(f\"unreadable document: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n    95\t    if len(text) > MAX_TEXT_CHARS:\n    96\t        raise Rejected(\"extracted text too long\")\n    97\t    if doc.media_type in SCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    98\t        findings = scan_for_injection(text)\n    99\t        if findings:\n   100\t            raise Rejected(\"possible prompt injection: \" + \"; \".join(findings))\n   101\t    return text\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t@router.post(\"/ingest/mail\")\n   105\tasync def ingest_mail(request: Request) -> dict:\n   106\t    body = await request.body()\n   107\t    if len(body) > MAX_BODY_BYTES * 2:\n   108\t        raise HTTPException(413, \"payload too large\")\n   109\t    key = Path(request.app.state.settings.mail_gateway_hmac_path).read_bytes().strip()\n   110\t    try:\n   111\t        verify_signature(\n   112\t            key,\n   113\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Timestamp\", \"\"),\n   114\t            body,\n   115\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Signature\", \"\"),\n   116\t        )\n   117\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   118\t        raise HTTPException(401, str(exc)) from exc\n   119\t\n   120\t    payload = await request.json()\n   121\t    doc = Inbound(\n   122\t        business_unit=payload[\"business_unit\"],\n   123\t        sender=payload[\"from\"],\n   124\t        media_type=payload[\"media_type\"],\n   125\t        raw=base64.b64decode(payload[\"content_b64\"], validate=True),\n   126\t    )\n   127\t    doc_id = f\"doc-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:20]}\"\n   128\t    pool = request.app.state.pool\n   129\t    try:\n   130\t        text = validate(doc)\n   131\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   132\t        await pool.execute(\n   133\t            \"\"\"\n   134\t            INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, reject_reason, received_at)\n   135\t            VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'quarantined', $6, now())\n   136\t            \"\"\",\n   137\t            doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   138\t            hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), str(exc)[:500],\n   139\t        )\n   140\t        return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"quarantined\"}\n   141\t\n   142\t    await pool.execute(\n   143\t        \"\"\"\n   144\t        INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, text, received_at)\n   145\t        VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'accepted', $6, now())\n   146\t        \"\"\",\n   147\t        doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   148\t        hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), text,\n   149\t    )\n   150\t    return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"accepted\"}\n=== app/killswitch.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Operator stop control.\n     2\t\n     3\tOperators halt the fleet or one business unit by setting a row in\n     4\t``control_flags`` with the ``procurement_ops`` database role (see\n     5\tops/README in the platform runbook). The agent's own database role has\n     6\tSELECT only on this table, so the agent cannot clear or delay a halt.\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\t\n    11\tclass AgentHalted(Exception):\n    12\t    pass\n    13\t\n    14\t\n    15\t_QUERY = \"\"\"\n    16\tSELECT scope, reason, set_by, set_at\n    17\tFROM control_flags\n    18\tWHERE halted\n    19\t  AND (scope = 'fleet' OR scope = $1)\n    20\tORDER BY CASE WHEN scope = 'fleet' THEN 0 ELSE 1 END\n    21\tLIMIT 1\n    22\t\"\"\"\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tasync def assert_running(pool, tenant: str) -> None:\n    26\t    row = await pool.fetchrow(_QUERY, f\"tenant:{tenant}\")\n    27\t    if row is not None:\n    28\t        raise AgentHalted(\n    29\t            f\"halted by {row['set_by']} at {row['set_at'].isoformat()} \"\n    30\t            f\"(scope={row['scope']}): {row['reason']}\"\n    31\t        )\n=== app/loop.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Procurement agent run loop.\n     2\t\n     3\tGraph: model turn -> (tool calls -> gate -> integration)* -> model turn ...\n     4\tEvery edge writes an audit node before the next step runs. Budgets are\n     5\tchecked before each model turn and each tool call.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\timport hashlib\n    10\timport logging\n    11\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n    12\tfrom typing import Any\n    13\t\n    14\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    15\t\n    16\tfrom app import audit, killswitch\n    17\tfrom app.budget import Budget, BudgetExceeded\n    18\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure, measure_context\n    19\tfrom app.gate import PolicyGate\n    20\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n    22\tfrom app.tools import ToolRegistry, build_registry\n    23\t\n    24\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    25\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.loop\")\n    26\t\n    27\tCOMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES = 40\n    28\tKEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES = 12\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t@dataclass\n    32\tclass AgentDeps:\n    33\t    settings: Any\n    34\t    pool: Any\n    35\t    gate: PolicyGate\n    36\t    erp: Any\n    37\t    slack: Any\n    38\t    broker: Any\n    39\t    extractor: Any = None\n    40\t    _budgets: dict[str, Budget] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    41\t    _contexts: dict[str, ContextMeasure] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    42\t\n    43\t    def current_budget(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> Budget:\n    44\t        return self._budgets[ident.run_id]\n    45\t\n    46\t    def current_context(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> ContextMeasure:\n    47\t        return self._contexts.get(ident.agent_instance_id, ContextMeasure.unavailable())\n    48\t\n    49\t    def erp_scope_for(self, operation: str) -> str:\n    50\t        scopes = self.settings.policy[\"erp\"][\"operation_scopes\"]\n    51\t        return scopes.get(operation, \"erp.read\")\n    52\t\n    53\t    async def execute_tool(self, ident, registry: ToolRegistry, use, parent: str, ctx: ContextMeasure) -> dict:\n    54\t        self._contexts[ident.agent_instance_id] = ctx\n    55\t        proposed = await audit.record(\n    56\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_proposed\", parent=parent, context=ctx,\n    57\t            payload={\"tool\": use.name, \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"args\": audit.summarize_args(use.input)},\n    58\t        )\n    59\t        tool = registry.get(use.name)\n    60\t        if tool is None:\n    61\t            await audit.record(\n    62\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_denied\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n    63\t                policy_version=self.gate.version, payload={\"reason\": \"tool not in role allowlist\"},\n    64\t            )\n    65\t            return _error(use.id, f\"tool {use.name} is not available to this agent\")\n    66\t\n    67\t        decision = await self.gate.authorize(ident, tool, use.input)\n    68\t        authz = await audit.record(\n    69\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"authz_decision\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n    70\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n    71\t            payload={\"allow\": decision.allow, \"reason\": decision.reason, \"pending\": decision.pending},\n    72\t        )\n    73\t        if not decision.allow:\n    74\t            if decision.pending:\n    75\t                return _error(use.id, f\"approval requested ({decision.approval_id}); do not retry until approved\")\n    76\t            return _error(use.id, f\"denied: {decision.reason}\")\n    77\t\n    78\t        operation_id = f\"op-{hashlib.sha256((authz + use.id).encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}\"\n    79\t        try:\n    80\t            with tracer.start_as_current_span(f\"execute_tool {use.name}\") as span:\n    81\t                for k, v in ctx.otel_attributes().items():\n    82\t                    span.set_attribute(k, v)\n    83\t                output = await tool.invoke(use.input, ident)\n    84\t        except BudgetExceeded:\n    85\t            raise\n    86\t        except Exception as exc:\n    87\t            await audit.record(\n    88\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_error\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n    89\t                policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n    90\t                operation_id=operation_id,\n    91\t                payload={\"error_type\": type(exc).__name__, \"error\": str(exc)[:500]},\n    92\t            )\n    93\t            return _error(use.id, f\"{use.name} failed: {type(exc).__name__}\")\n    94\t\n    95\t        await audit.record(\n    96\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_result\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n    97\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n    98\t            operation_id=operation_id,\n    99\t            payload={\"result_sha256\": audit.digest(output), \"result\": output},\n   100\t        )\n   101\t        return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"content\": redact_for_model(output)}\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\tdef _error(tool_use_id: str, message: str) -> dict:\n   105\t    return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": tool_use_id, \"is_error\": True, \"content\": message}\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef _compact(messages: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], bool]:\n   109\t    if len(messages) <= COMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES:\n   110\t        return messages, False\n   111\t    head, tail = messages[:1], messages[-KEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES:]\n   112\t    while tail and tail[0][\"role\"] != \"assistant\":\n   113\t        tail = tail[1:]\n   114\t    note = {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[earlier tool exchanges were removed to save space]\"}\n   115\t    return head + [note] + tail, True\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\tclass ProcurementAgent:\n   119\t    def __init__(self, *, client, deps: AgentDeps, system_prompt: str, role: str = \"procurement\"):\n   120\t        self.client = client\n   121\t        self.deps = deps\n   122\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n   123\t        self.role = role\n   124\t\n   125\t    async def run(self, ident: RunIdentity, task: str) -> str | None:\n   126\t        pool = self.deps.pool\n   127\t        await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n   128\t        budget = Budget.for_run(self.deps.settings.budgets, ident)\n   129\t        await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n   130\t        self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n   131\t        registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n   132\t\n   133\t        run_node = await audit.record(\n   134\t            pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n   135\t            payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n   136\t        )\n   137\t        messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n   138\t        try:\n   139\t            while True:\n   140\t                budget.check_step()\n   141\t                messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\n   142\t                request = {\n   143\t                    \"model\": self.deps.settings.model_id,\n   144\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n   145\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n   146\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n   147\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n   148\t                }\n   149\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted)\n   150\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n   151\t                budget.charge_model(self.deps.settings.model_id, response.usage)\n   152\t                await budget.flush(pool)\n   153\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n   154\t                decision = await audit.record(\n   155\t                    pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n   156\t                    payload={\n   157\t                        \"requested_model\": request[\"model\"],\n   158\t                        \"served_model\": response.model,\n   159\t                        \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason,\n   160\t                        \"proposed_tools\": [b.name for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"],\n   161\t                    },\n   162\t                )\n   163\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n   164\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n   165\t                if not uses:\n   166\t                    final = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n   167\t                    await audit.record(pool, ident, kind=\"run_finished\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n   168\t                                       payload={\"final_sha256\": audit.digest(final)})\n   169\t                    return final\n   170\t                results = []\n   171\t                for use in uses:\n   172\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n   173\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n   174\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n   175\t        except BudgetExceeded as exc:\n   176\t            await audit.record(\n   177\t                pool, ident, kind=\"budget_exceeded\", parent=run_node,\n   178\t                payload={\"limit\": exc.limit, \"used\": str(exc.used), \"allowed\": str(exc.allowed)},\n   179\t            )\n   180\t            await self.deps.slack.post(\n   181\t                channel=\"#procurement-agent-ops\",\n   182\t                text=f\"Run {ident.run_id} ({ident.tenant}) stopped: {exc.limit} exceeded.\",\n   183\t            )\n   184\t            return None\n   185\t        finally:\n   186\t            self.deps._budgets.pop(ident.run_id, None)\n=== app/main.py\n     1\t\"\"\"FastAPI entry point for the procurement agent.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport asyncio\n     5\timport hashlib\n     6\timport hmac\n     7\timport json\n     8\timport logging\n     9\timport time\n    10\timport uuid\n    11\tfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\n    12\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    13\tfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs\n    14\t\n    15\timport asyncpg\n    16\timport jwt\n    17\tfrom anthropic import AsyncAnthropic\n    18\tfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, HTTPException, Request\n    19\tfrom fastapi.security import HTTPAuthorizationCredentials, HTTPBearer\n    20\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    21\tfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n    22\t\n    23\tfrom app import audit, ingest\n    24\tfrom app.approvals import ApprovalStore, ApproverNotAuthorized\n    25\tfrom app.extractor import LineItemExtractor\n    26\tfrom app.gate import PolicyGate\n    27\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity, TokenBroker, new_instance_id\n    28\tfrom app.loop import AgentDeps, ProcurementAgent\n    29\tfrom app.mcp_client import ErpMcpClient\n    30\tfrom app.redact import RedactingFilter\n    31\tfrom app.settings import get_settings\n    32\tfrom app.startup import startup_checks\n    33\tfrom app.tools.slack import SlackClient\n    34\t\n    35\tlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\"%(asctime)s %(levelname)s %(name)s %(message)s\")\n    36\tfor handler in logging.getLogger().handlers:\n    37\t    handler.addFilter(RedactingFilter())\n    38\tlog = logging.getLogger(\"procurement\")\n    39\t\n    40\tAGENT_PRINCIPAL = \"spiffe://example-corp.test/ns/procurement-prod/sa/procurement-agent\"\n    41\tbearer = HTTPBearer()\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\tclass RunRequest(BaseModel):\n    45\t    task: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=4000)\n    46\t    department: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=64)\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tclass Principal(BaseModel):\n    50\t    subject: str\n    51\t    business_unit: str\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef service_identity(settings, agent_type_id: str, tenant: str = \"system\") -> RunIdentity:\n    55\t    return RunIdentity(\n    56\t        accountable_party=\"system:procurement-agent\",\n    57\t        operational_owner=settings.operational_owner,\n    58\t        tenant=tenant,\n    59\t        agent_type_id=agent_type_id,\n    60\t        agent_instance_id=new_instance_id(),\n    61\t        trace_id=uuid.uuid4().hex,\n    62\t        run_id=f\"bg-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n    63\t        delegated_subject=\"system:procurement-agent\",\n    64\t        agent_principal=AGENT_PRINCIPAL,\n    65\t    )\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\tasync def expire_approvals_forever(app: FastAPI) -> None:\n    69\t    while True:\n    70\t        await asyncio.sleep(60)\n    71\t        ident = service_identity(app.state.settings, app.state.agent_type_id)\n    72\t        count = await app.state.pool.fetchval(\n    73\t            \"WITH e AS (UPDATE approvals SET status = 'expired' \"\n    74\t            \"WHERE status = 'pending' AND expires_at <= now() RETURNING 1) SELECT count(*) FROM e\"\n    75\t        )\n    76\t        await audit.record(app.state.pool, ident, kind=\"background_job\",\n    77\t                           payload={\"job\": \"expire_approvals\", \"expired\": count})\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t@asynccontextmanager\n    81\tasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    82\t    settings = get_settings()\n    83\t    agent_type_id = startup_checks(settings)\n    84\t    pool = await asyncpg.create_pool(settings.database_url, min_size=2, max_size=10)\n    85\t    broker = TokenBroker(settings)\n    86\t\n    87\t    async def slack_token() -> str:\n    88\t        return await broker.token_for(\"slack-proxy\", \"chat:write\", service_identity(settings, agent_type_id))\n    89\t\n    90\t    slack = SlackClient(settings.slack_api_url, slack_token)\n    91\t    approvals = ApprovalStore(pool, settings.policy, slack)\n    92\t    gate = PolicyGate(settings.policy, approvals)\n    93\t    erp = ErpMcpClient(settings.erp_mcp_url, settings.manifest[\"tool_pins\"], broker)\n    94\t    await erp.initialize(service_identity(settings, agent_type_id))\n    95\t\n    96\t    client = AsyncAnthropic()\n    97\t    deps = AgentDeps(settings=settings, pool=pool, gate=gate, erp=erp, slack=slack, broker=broker)\n    98\t    deps.extractor = LineItemExtractor(\n    99\t        client=client, settings=settings, deps=deps,\n   100\t        system_prompt=(settings.prompt_dir / \"extractor.md\").read_text(),\n   101\t    )\n   102\t    app.state.settings = settings\n   103\t    app.state.pool = pool\n   104\t    app.state.agent_type_id = agent_type_id\n   105\t    app.state.approvals = approvals\n   106\t    app.state.agent = ProcurementAgent(\n   107\t        client=client, deps=deps, system_prompt=(settings.prompt_dir / \"system.md\").read_text()\n   108\t    )\n   109\t    app.state.jwks = jwt.PyJWKClient(settings.oidc_jwks_url, cache_keys=True, lifespan=300)\n   110\t    sweeper = asyncio.create_task(expire_approvals_forever(app))\n   111\t    try:\n   112\t        yield\n   113\t    finally:\n   114\t        sweeper.cancel()\n   115\t        await pool.close()\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\tapp = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)\n   119\tapp.include_router(ingest.router)\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef authenticate(request: Request, creds: HTTPAuthorizationCredentials = Depends(bearer)) -> Principal:\n   123\t    settings = request.app.state.settings\n   124\t    try:\n   125\t        key = request.app.state.jwks.get_signing_key_from_jwt(creds.credentials)\n   126\t        claims = jwt.decode(\n   127\t            creds.credentials,\n   128\t            key.key,\n   129\t            algorithms=[\"RS256\", \"ES256\"],\n   130\t            audience=settings.oidc_audience,\n   131\t            issuer=settings.oidc_issuer,\n   132\t            options={\"require\": [\"exp\", \"iat\", \"sub\", \"aud\", \"iss\"]},\n   133\t        )\n   134\t    except jwt.PyJWTError as exc:\n   135\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"invalid token\") from exc\n   136\t    bu = claims.get(\"bu\")\n   137\t    if not bu:\n   138\t        raise HTTPException(403, \"token has no business unit\")\n   139\t    return Principal(subject=claims[\"sub\"], business_unit=bu)\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t@app.post(\"/runs\")\n   143\tasync def start_run(req: RunRequest, request: Request, principal: Principal = Depends(authenticate)) -> dict:\n   144\t    settings = request.app.state.settings\n   145\t    span_ctx = trace.get_current_span().get_span_context()\n   146\t    trace_id = format(span_ctx.trace_id, \"032x\") if span_ctx.is_valid else uuid.uuid4().hex\n   147\t    ident = RunIdentity(\n   148\t        accountable_party=principal.subject,\n   149\t        operational_owner=settings.operational_owner,\n   150\t        tenant=principal.business_unit,\n   151\t        agent_type_id=request.app.state.agent_type_id,\n   152\t        agent_instance_id=new_instance_id(),\n   153\t        trace_id=trace_id,\n   154\t        run_id=f\"run-{uuid.uuid4()}\",\n   155\t        delegated_subject=principal.subject,\n   156\t        agent_principal=AGENT_PRINCIPAL,\n   157\t    )\n   158\t    task = f\"Department: {req.department}\\n\\n{req.task}\"\n   159\t    asyncio.create_task(request.app.state.agent.run(ident, task))\n   160\t    return {\"run_id\": ident.run_id, \"agent_instance_id\": ident.agent_instance_id}\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t@app.post(\"/slack/interactions\")\n   164\tasync def slack_interactions(request: Request) -> dict:\n   165\t    body = await request.body()\n   166\t    timestamp = request.headers.get(\"X-Slack-Request-Timestamp\", \"0\")\n   167\t    if abs(time.time() - int(timestamp)) > 300:\n   168\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"stale request\")\n   169\t    secret = Path(request.app.state.settings.slack_signing_secret_path).read_bytes().strip()\n   170\t    expected = \"v0=\" + hmac.new(secret, f\"v0:{timestamp}:\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n   171\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, request.headers.get(\"X-Slack-Signature\", \"\")):\n   172\t        raise HTTPException(401, \"bad signature\")\n   173\t\n   174\t    payload = json.loads(parse_qs(body.decode())[\"payload\"][0])\n   175\t    action = payload[\"actions\"][0]\n   176\t    slack_user = payload[\"user\"][\"id\"]\n   177\t    row = await request.app.state.pool.fetchrow(\n   178\t        \"SELECT email, role FROM approvers WHERE slack_user_id = $1 AND active\", slack_user\n   179\t    )\n   180\t    if row is None:\n   181\t        raise HTTPException(403, \"not an approver\")\n   182\t    try:\n   183\t        await request.app.state.approvals.decide(\n   184\t            action[\"value\"], approver=row[\"email\"], approver_role=row[\"role\"],\n   185\t            approve=action[\"action_id\"] == \"approve\",\n   186\t        )\n   187\t    except ApproverNotAuthorized as exc:\n   188\t        raise HTTPException(403, str(exc)) from exc\n   189\t    except ValueError as exc:\n   190\t        raise HTTPException(409, str(exc)) from exc\n   191\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t@app.get(\"/healthz\")\n   195\tasync def healthz() -> dict:\n   196\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n=== app/mcp_client.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Client for the ERP MCP server, reached through the internal MCP gateway.\n     2\t\n     3\tOn startup the tool list is fetched and each tool's description and input\n     4\tschema are fingerprinted and compared with the pins in the release manifest.\n     5\tAny unpinned or changed tool stops startup. Tool metadata is also scanned for\n     6\tinstruction-like content before any of it is shown to the model.\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport hashlib\n    11\timport json\n    12\timport logging\n    13\timport re\n    14\timport uuid\n    15\tfrom typing import Any\n    16\t\n    17\timport httpx\n    18\t\n    19\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity, TokenBroker\n    20\tfrom app.redact import redact_text\n    21\t\n    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    23\t\n    24\tMAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS = 1024\n    25\tSUSPICIOUS_METADATA = [\n    26\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|previous|prior) instructions\"),\n    27\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are now|act as)\\b\"),\n    28\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(before|instead of) (calling|using) \\w+\\.\\w+\"),\n    29\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n    30\t    re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\"),\n    31\t]\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tclass ToolPinMismatch(Exception):\n    35\t    pass\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tclass UnknownErpOperation(Exception):\n    39\t    pass\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef fingerprint(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    43\t    material = {\n    44\t        \"name\": tool[\"name\"],\n    45\t        \"description\": tool.get(\"description\", \"\"),\n    46\t        \"inputSchema\": tool.get(\"inputSchema\", {}),\n    47\t        \"annotations\": tool.get(\"annotations\", {}),\n    48\t    }\n    49\t    raw = json.dumps(material, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n    50\t    return \"sha256:\" + hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tdef scan_metadata(tool: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    54\t    description = tool.get(\"description\", \"\")\n    55\t    if len(description) > MAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS:\n    56\t        raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: description too long\")\n    57\t    blob = json.dumps(tool, ensure_ascii=False)\n    58\t    for pattern in SUSPICIOUS_METADATA:\n    59\t        if pattern.search(blob):\n    60\t            raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: suspicious metadata ({pattern.pattern})\")\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tclass ErpMcpClient:\n    64\t    AUDIENCE = \"erp-mcp-gateway\"\n    65\t\n    66\t    def __init__(self, url: str, pins: dict[str, str], broker: TokenBroker):\n    67\t        self.url = url\n    68\t        self.pins = pins\n    69\t        self.broker = broker\n    70\t        self._tools: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    71\t\n    72\t    async def _rpc(self, method: str, params: dict[str, Any], token: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    73\t        async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=20.0, follow_redirects=False) as client:\n    74\t            resp = await client.post(\n    75\t                self.url,\n    76\t                json={\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": str(uuid.uuid4()), \"method\": method, \"params\": params},\n    77\t                headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Mcp-Protocol-Version\": \"2025-06-18\"},\n    78\t            )\n    79\t        resp.raise_for_status()\n    80\t        if len(resp.content) > 512_000:\n    81\t            raise ValueError(\"erp response too large\")\n    82\t        body = resp.json()\n    83\t        if \"error\" in body:\n    84\t            raise RuntimeError(f\"erp error {body['error'].get('code')}: {redact_text(str(body['error'].get('message')))}\")\n    85\t        return body[\"result\"]\n    86\t\n    87\t    async def _list_tools(self, token: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    88\t        result = await self._rpc(\"tools/list\", {}, token)\n    89\t        return list(result.get(\"tools\", []))\n    90\t\n    91\t    async def initialize(self, service_ident: RunIdentity) -> None:\n    92\t        token = await self.broker.token_for(self.AUDIENCE, \"erp.tools.list\", service_ident)\n    93\t        tools = await self._list_tools(token)\n    94\t        for tool in tools:\n    95\t            expected = self.pins.get(tool[\"name\"])\n    96\t            actual = fingerprint(tool)\n    97\t            if expected != actual:\n    98\t                raise ToolPinMismatch(f\"{tool['name']}: expected {expected}, got {actual}\")\n    99\t            scan_metadata(tool)\n   100\t        self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}\n   101\t        log.info(\"erp tools loaded: %d\", len(self._tools))\n   102\t\n   103\t    async def on_notification(self, message: dict[str, Any], service_ident: RunIdentity) -> None:\n   104\t        if message.get(\"method\") == \"notifications/tools/list_changed\":\n   105\t            await self.refresh_tools(service_ident)\n   106\t\n   107\t    async def refresh_tools(self, service_ident: RunIdentity) -> None:\n   108\t        token = await self.broker.token_for(self.AUDIENCE, \"erp.tools.list\", service_ident)\n   109\t        tools = await self._list_tools(token)\n   110\t        self._tools = {t[\"name\"]: t for t in tools}\n   111\t        log.info(\"erp tools refreshed: %d\", len(self._tools))\n   112\t\n   113\t    def operations(self) -> list[str]:\n   114\t        return sorted(self._tools)\n   115\t\n   116\t    async def call(self, operation: str, arguments: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity, scope: str) -> Any:\n   117\t        if operation not in self._tools:\n   118\t            raise UnknownErpOperation(operation)\n   119\t        token = await self.broker.token_for(self.AUDIENCE, scope, ident)\n   120\t        result = await self._rpc(\n   121\t            \"tools/call\",\n   122\t            {\n   123\t                \"name\": operation,\n   124\t                \"arguments\": arguments,\n   125\t                \"_meta\": {\"business_unit\": ident.tenant, \"run_id\": ident.run_id},\n   126\t            },\n   127\t            token,\n   128\t        )\n   129\t        if result.get(\"isError\"):\n   130\t            raise RuntimeError(redact_text(json.dumps(result.get(\"content\", []))))\n   131\t        return result.get(\"structuredContent\") or result.get(\"content\")\n=== app/redact.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Redaction for model input, logs, audit payloads, and outbound messages.\n     2\t\n     3\tApplied in four places:\n     4\t  * tool results before they are appended to the model context (loop.py)\n     5\t  * every audit payload (audit.py)\n     6\t  * the root logging filter (main.py)\n     7\t  * outbound Slack text (tools/slack.py)\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations","numLines":900,"startLine":700,"totalLines":2366}}}
